t["subzone:blackwolf-river"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,259,17.458.0,46.133.0,32.203.0,43.194.0",["h"]="fef9c7",["n"]="Río Lobonegro",["s"]="Río Lobonegro. El Río Lobonegro es un curso de agua que nace en el Lago del Peñasco y desciende a través del Risco Cortaviento en Sierra Espolón. Antaño un arroyo de montaña limpio, sus aguas han acabado totalmente contaminadas por la agresiva tala y las operaciones industriales de Ventura y Cía. Al descender del Lago del Peñasco, el Río Lobonegro atraviesa la cuenca del Risco Cortaviento. Lo que debería ser un afluente alpino prístino ha sufrido en su lugar el impacto de la desenfrenada iniciativa goblin. A medida que Ventura y Cía. tala los bosques circundantes con maquinaria pesada y sierras circulares, lodos, petróleo y residuos de la tala se filtran de forma constante en la corriente. El río despojado se erige como un claro ejemplo del expolio comercial que amenaza las tierras salvajes de Sierra Espolón.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="The desecration of Blackwolf River by goblin timber operations is a sharp affront to the Cenarion Circle and all who revere the untamed waters of Kalimdor.",["race:Tauren"]="Seeing the earth scarred and the waters fouled by profit-driven interlopers reinforces the tauren resolve to cleanse Stonetalon of reckless industrial blight."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The river flows down out of Cragpool Lake in the upper reaches of the mountains and winds through the logged basin of Windshear Crag.",["al"]={"blackwolf river source","where is blackwolf river","blackwolf river location"},["q"]="Where does the Blackwolf River start and lead?"},{["a"]="The Venture Company operates massive deforestation and mechanical logging rigs throughout Windshear Crag. Runoff from their steam machinery, waste, and clear-cutting drains directly into the watercourse.",["al"]={"why is blackwolf river dirty","blackwolf river pollution","venture company pollution"},["q"]="Why is the river water polluted?"},{["a"]="The Venture Company dominates the riverbank, utilizing the surrounding valley for heavy lumber harvesting and mechanical operations despite resistance from local wildlife and native inhabitants.",["al"]={"who controls blackwolf river","who is at blackwolf river","enemies near blackwolf river"},["q"]="Who is currently operating along the river?"}},["kw"]={"blackwolf river","cragpool lake","logging","pollution","stonetalon mountains","venture co","venture company","windshear crag"},["n"]="Blackwolf River",["s"]="Blackwolf River is a waterway flowing out of Cragpool Lake down through Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains. Once a clean mountain stream, its waters have become thoroughly polluted by the Venture Company's aggressive logging and industrial operations.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Descending from Cragpool Lake, the Blackwolf River cuts across the basin of Windshear Crag. What should be a pristine alpine tributary has instead borne the brunt of unchecked goblin enterprise. As the Venture Company clears the surrounding woodlands with heavy machinery and buzzsaws, sludge, oil, and logging waste leach steadily into the current. The despoiled river stands as a vivid example of the commercial plunder threatening Stonetalon's wilderness.",["t"]="Industrial Runoff"}}}}}
t["subzone:blackwood-den"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,344,22.482.0,22.186.0,40.208.0,34.231.0",["h"]="a5add9",["n"]="Cubil del Bosque Negro",["s"]="Cubil del Bosque Negro. El Cubil del Bosque Negro es un campamento de fúrbolgs corrompidos situado en los confines meridionales de Costa Oscura, cerca de la frontera con Vallefresno. La cueva y los campamentos circundantes, que antaño fueron un asentamiento pacífico, han sucumbido a la locura junto al resto de la tribu Bosque Negro. Un solitario explorador elfo de la noche llamado Volcor se encuentra atrapado en el interior de la caverna, a la espera de recibir ayuda desde Auberdine. Situado cerca de la frontera sur, donde Costa Oscura se une con Vallefresno, el Cubil del Bosque Negro está formado por una serpenteante red de toscos campamentos y una cueva rocosa. Los fúrbolgs Bosque Negro que moran aquí han sucumbido a la omnipresente corrupción que azota la región, volviéndose violentamente hostiles hacia los forasteros. En las profundidades de la cueva del cubil, el elfo de la noche Volcor permanece acorralado y en peligro por culpa de la agresiva tribu, necesitando con desesperación la ayuda de exploradores y viajeros enviados desde Auberdine.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Druids mourn the fall of the furbolgs, who were once steadfast protectors of the wilderness, and view the madness at Blackwood Den as another painful symptom of Kalimdor's tainted nature.",["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves of Auberdine, the loss of the Blackwood tribe to corruption is a tragic development, and rescuing Volcor from their clutches is an urgent duty to keep their people safe along the southern road."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Blackwood Den is a furbolg settlement and cave complex located in far southern Darkshore, close to the border of Ashenvale. It serves as a base for the corrupted Blackwood furbolg tribe.",["al"]={"what is blackwood den","blackwood hold","where is blackwood den"},["q"]="What is Blackwood Den?"},{["a"]="Inside the cave sits Volcor, a night elf who has become trapped behind enemy lines. Travelers who encounter him must coordinate with allies in Auberdine to stage an escape and guide him safely out of the den.",["al"]={"who is trapped in the cave","who is volcor","elf in blackwood den"},["q"]="Who is inside the cave at Blackwood Den?"},{["a"]="The Blackwood furbolgs have fallen victim to the dark corruption spreading across Darkshore and Kalimdor following the Third War. The affliction has driven them into a maddened frenzy, causing them to attack any outsiders on sight.",["al"]={"why are blackwood furbolgs aggressive","are blackwood furbolgs evil","corrupted furbolgs darkshore"},["q"]="Why are the furbolgs here hostile?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","auberdine","blackwood den","blackwood hold","darkshore","furbolg","volcor"},["n"]="Blackwood Den",["s"]="Blackwood Den is a corrupted furbolg encampment nestled in the southern reaches of Darkshore near the border of Ashenvale. Once a peaceful dwelling, the cave and surrounding camps have fallen into madness alongside the rest of the Blackwood tribe. A lone night elf scout named Volcor sits trapped within the cavern, awaiting aid from Auberdine.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated near the southern border where Darkshore meets Ashenvale, Blackwood Den consists of a winding network of crude camps and a rocky cave. The Blackwood furbolgs who dwell here have succumbed to the pervasive corruption gripping the region, turning violently hostile toward outsiders. Deep inside the den's cave, the night elf Volcor remains pinned down and endangered by the aggressive tribe, desperately needing assistance from scouts and travelers dispatched from Auberdine.",["t"]="A Corrupted Stronghold"}}}}}
t["subzone:bladefist-bay"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,267,25.553.0,28.387.0,33.157.0,31.129.0,39.148.0,46.175.0",["h"]="aab6b1",["n"]="Bahía de Garrafilada",["s"]="Bahía de Garrafilada. La Bahía de Garrafilada es el escarpado tramo de costa que bordea el este de Durotar, justo a las puertas de Orgrimmar. Bautizada en honor a Kargath Garrafilada, la bahía sirve como un puerto natural frente al Mare Magnum, a la sombra de riscos escarpados y de las cercanas costas meridionales de Azshara. Extendiéndose a lo largo del extremo nororiental de Durotar, la Bahía de Garrafilada se abre directamente a las vastas aguas del Mare Magnum. Flanqueada por acantilados rocosos y un oleaje traicionero, funciona como un umbral marítimo primordial para la capital de la Horda, Orgrimmar. Las mareas depositan con frecuencia madera flotante, desperdicios marinos y restos de naufragios en la costa, lo que le ha valido entre los lugareños la reputación de ser un punto de recolección natural de restos oceánicos. Directamente al norte, los antiguos acantilados rojos y las ruinas de Azshara se alzan al otro lado del agua, convirtiendo a la bahía en una frontera marítima vital para Durotar.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="The Shattered Hand operates within Orgrimmar's shadows as the Horde's guild of thieves and assassins, giving this coast quiet resonance for covert operatives.",["race:Orc"]="The bay bears the proud and brutal name of Kargath Bladefist, serving as a reminder of the trials of the Shattered Hand clan on Draenor."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The bay is named after Kargath Bladefist, the legendary chieftain of the Shattered Hand clan known for replacing his severed hand with a lethal scythe blade.",["al"]={"who is bladefist","bladefist namesake","kargath bladefist bay"},["q"]="Who is Bladefist Bay named after?"},{["a"]="It lies along the northeastern coast of Durotar, directly east of Orgrimmar's main gates and south across the water from Azshara.",["al"]={"bladefist bay location","where is bladefist bay","how to get to bladefist bay"},["q"]="Where is Bladefist Bay located?"},{["a"]="The shoreline is situated right beside Skull Rock, a cavern infamous for harboring warlocks, demons, and members of the sinister Burning Blade cult.",["al"]={"bladefist bay danger","dangers at bladefist bay","enemies in bladefist bay"},["q"]="What threats lurk around Bladefist Bay?"},{["a"]="Ocean currents from the Great Sea routinely sweep sea detritus, wreckage, and rubble straight onto its shores, giving it a reputation as a dumping ground for the sea's refuse.",["al"]={"midden heap","bladefist flotsam","ocean trash bay"},["q"]="Why is the bay sometimes called a midden heap?"}},["kw"]={"bay","bladefist","durotar","great sea","kargath","orgrimmar","shattered hand","skull rock"},["n"]="Bladefist Bay",["s"]="Bladefist Bay is the rugged stretch of coast lining eastern Durotar just outside the gates of Orgrimmar. Named in honor of Kargath Bladefist, the bay serves as a natural harbor facing the Great Sea, shadowed by craggy bluffs and the nearby southern shores of Azshara.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Stretching along the northeastern edge of Durotar, Bladefist Bay opens directly into the vast waters of the Great Sea. Flanked by rocky cliffs and treacherous surf, it functions as a primary maritime threshold for the Horde capital of Orgrimmar. The tides frequently deposit driftwood, ocean refuse, and flotsam onto the coastline, earning it a reputation among locals as a natural collection point for ocean debris. Directly north, the ancient red cliffs and ruins of Azshara loom across the water, making the bay a vital maritime boundary for Durotar.",["t"]="A Harbor on the Great Sea"},{["b"]="The bay honors Kargath Bladefist, the famed chieftain of the Shattered Hand clan who severed his own hand to replace it with a blade during the old Horde's trials on Draenor. The proximity of the bay to places like Skull Rock—where cultists and hidden rogue networks operate in the shadows—echoes the fierce and ruthless legacy of the clan whose chieftain gave the waters their name.",["t"]="Shadow of the Shattered Hand"}}}}}
t["subzone:bloodhoof-village"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,379,19.417.0,20.454.0,28.141.0,36.160.0,43.146.0,55.142.0",["h"]="cfcc80",["n"]="Poblado Pezuña de Sangre",["s"]="Poblado Pezuña de Sangre. El Poblado Pezuña de Sangre es un asentamiento tauren central ubicado a orillas del Lago Toro de Piedra, en Mulgore. Bautizado en honor a la tribu Pezuña de Sangre, sirve como el primer gran núcleo de reunión para los jóvenes cazadores y bravos que viajan desde el Campamento Narache hacia Cima del Trueno. Dirigido por Baine Pezuña de Sangre, el poblado coordina la defensa local, el comercio y los ritos tradicionales por todas las llanuras. Situado en torno a las aguas cristalinas del Lago Toro de Piedra, el Poblado Pezuña de Sangre es un bullicioso centro de comercio, artesanía y ceremonias en el centro de Mulgore. Los jóvenes tauren que concluyen sus pruebas en el Campamento Narache llegan aquí para perfeccionar sus habilidades antes de aventurarse hacia las grandes mesetas de Cima del Trueno. También es muy conocido en todo Kalimdor por sus maestros constructores de tambores y por los pacientes criadores que domestican kodos salvajes para el transporte.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="This peaceful settlement serves as a critical stopover and logistics link between the southern plains of Mulgore and the Horde capital at Thunder Bluff.",["race:Tauren"]="For young tauren, entering Bloodhoof Village marks the first real step beyond youth into broader tribal responsibility and spiritual maturity."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Baine Bloodhoof, son of High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof, leads the settlement and directs its defenses against threats to the central plains.",["al"]={"village leader","baine bloodhoof location","who is in charge of bloodhoof village"},["q"]="Who leads Bloodhoof Village?"},{["a"]="Spiritual advisors such as Zarlman Two-Moons guide young tauren through the traditional Rite of Vision, an essential spiritual journey on the path to adulthood.",["al"]={"rite of vision","spiritual trials","zarlman two-moons quest"},["q"]="What major rites are conducted here?"},{["a"]="Bloodhoof Village is famed for its uniquely crafted ceremony drums and is the primary hub where wild plains kodos are tamed and trained as mounts.",["al"]={"tauren mounts","kodo taming","bloodhoof drums"},["q"]="What is the settlement known for producing?"},{["a"]="Once their deeds in central Mulgore are complete, travelers are generally directed northward to Thunder Bluff, the capital city of the tauren.",["al"]={"after bloodhoof","where next after bloodhoof","next hub"},["q"]="Where do travelers go after finishing their tasks here?"}},["kw"]={"baine bloodhoof","bloodhoof village","camp narache","kodo","mulgore","stonebull lake","zarlman two-moons"},["n"]="Bloodhoof Village",["s"]="Bloodhoof Village is a central tauren settlement resting along the banks of Stonebull Lake in Mulgore. Named in honor of the Bloodhoof tribe, it serves as the first major gathering hub for young hunters and braves journeying out from Camp Narache toward Thunder Bluff. Led by Baine Bloodhoof, the village coordinates local defense, trade, and traditional rites across the plains.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated around the clear waters of Stonebull Lake, Bloodhoof Village is a bustling center of commerce, craft, and ceremony in central Mulgore. Young tauren departing their trials at Camp Narache arrive here to hone their skills before venturing onward to the great mesas of Thunder Bluff. It is also well-known across Kalimdor for its master drum makers and the patient breeders who tame wild kodo beasts for travel.",["t"]="Heart of the Plains"},{["b"]="Day-to-day governance and the defense of the region fall under Baine Bloodhoof, son of High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof. Under his watchful eye, braves are dispatched to secure the grasslands against aggressive wildlife, quilboar encroachers, and the shadowy presence of the Venture Company. Alongside Baine, spiritual guides such as Zarlman Two-Moons tend to the inner life of the tribe, directing novices through sacred journeys like the Rite of Vision.",["t"]="Leadership and Rites"}}}}}
t["subzone:bloodtooth-camp"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,364,15.448.0,20.375.1,33.131.0,34.213.0,42.131.0,39.222.0",["h"]="22e842",["n"]="Asentamiento Sangradientes",["s"]="Asentamiento Sangradientes. El Asentamiento Sangradientes es un campamento de fúrbolgs hostiles y corruptos ubicado en el centro de Vallefresno, situado justo al oeste del Río Falfarren. Lideradas por el cabecilla Ran Sangradientes, estas criaturas que antaño eran pacíficas han sucumbido a una oscura locura y atacan a cualquiera que se acerque. El campamento es un objetivo prioritario para los exploradores de la Alianza que trabajan para purificar los bosques circundantes. Enclavado al suroeste del Pozo de la Luna meridional y al oeste del Río Falfarren, el Asentamiento Sangradientes sirve como un crudo recordatorio de la creciente decadencia de Vallefresno. Los fúrbolgs que viven aquí estuvieron una vez conectados con la naturaleza sagrada de Kalimdor, pero una persistente corrupción espiritual ha consumido a su tribu. Bajo el mando de Ran Sangradientes, custodian su tosco poblado con una hostilidad rabiosa, arremetiendo tanto contra viajeros como contra protectores elfos de la noche.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance adventurers, Bloodtooth Camp represents a localized hotspot of corruption that threatens the safety of Ashenvale's southern groves and moonwells.",["race:NightElf"]="Night elves view the maddened state of Ran Bloodtooth's tribe as a tragic symptom of the deep corruption blighting their ancient ancestral homeland."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Bloodtooth Camp is situated in central Ashenvale, directly west of the Falfarren River and just southwest of the southern Moonwell.",["al"]={"bloodtooth camp location","where is bloodtooth camp","find bloodtooth camp"},["q"]="Where is Bloodtooth Camp located?"},{["a"]="Like many furbolg tribes across Ashenvale, the Bloodtooth clan has fallen victim to a dark demonic corruption lingering in the wilderness. It drives them into madness and boundless aggression toward all outsiders.",["al"]={"why are bloodtooth furbolgs attacking","bloodtooth corruption","are furbolgs evil here"},["q"]="Why are the furbolgs here hostile?"},{["a"]="The camp is ruled by Ran Bloodtooth, a fierce chieftain who commands the local furbolgs alongside his personal cadre of bodyguards.",["al"]={"bloodtooth camp boss","ran bloodtooth","who leads bloodtooth camp"},["q"]="Who leads the furbolgs at Bloodtooth Camp?"},{["a"]="During the efforts surrounding Raene's Cleansing, the exiled furbolg Krolg directs Alliance champions to strike at the encampment, eliminate Ran Bloodtooth, and remove the threat his corrupted followers pose to the region.",["al"]={"bloodtooth camp quest","why kill ran bloodtooth","krolg mission"},["q"]="Why does the Alliance send scouts here?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","bloodtooth camp","falfarren river","furbolg","krolg","raene's cleansing","ran bloodtooth"},["n"]="Bloodtooth Camp",["s"]="Bloodtooth Camp is an encampment of hostile, corrupted furbolgs tucked into central Ashenvale, situated just west of the Falfarren River. Led by the chieftain Ran Bloodtooth, these once-peaceful creatures have succumbed to dark madness and attack anyone who approaches. The camp is a primary target for Alliance scouts working to cleanse the surrounding woodlands.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Nestled southwest of the southern Moonwell and west of the Falfarren River, Bloodtooth Camp serves as a stark reminder of Ashenvale's encroaching decay. The furbolgs living here were once connected to the sacred wilderness of Kalimdor, but a lingering spiritual corruption has consumed their tribe. Under the command of Ran Bloodtooth, they guard their crude settlement with rabid hostility, turning upon travelers and night elven protectors alike.",["t"]="A Corrupted Den"},{["b"]="Because Ran Bloodtooth's band poses an immediate danger to nearby sacred sites, Alliance sentinels and their allies cannot ignore the camp. As part of efforts to restore harmony to the forest—namely aiding Raene Wolfrunner's cleansing endeavors—adventurers are directed by Krolg to infiltrate the camp, cut down Ran Bloodtooth, and put an end to his ferocious bodyguards.",["t"]="Cleansing the Forest"}}}}}
t["subzone:bough-shadow"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,221,22.577.0,38.210.0,44.246.0,32.176.0,29.162.0",["h"]="215295",["n"]="Talloumbrío",["s"]="Talloumbrío. Talloumbrío es una arboleda apartada escondida en el extremo noreste de Vallefresno, al este de Canción del Bosque. Se articula en torno a un colosal Gran Árbol cuyas raíces se asientan sobre un antiguo portal que conduce directamente a El Sueño Esmeralda. Talloumbrío alberga uno de los escasos Grandes Árboles nacidos a partir de un esqueje del Árbol del Mundo, Nordrassil. Plantado hace mucho tiempo por druidas seguidores de Fandral Corzocelada, sus raíces se hunden en las profundidades de la tierra alrededor de un cruce natural hacia El Sueño Esmeralda. En la actualidad, esta arboleda tranquila a la vez que imponente se halla fuertemente custodiada por el Vuelo del Dragón Verde. Dracos esmeralda como Phantim y Dreamstalker sobrevuelan las copas de los árboles, mientras que patrullas de dragonantes Emeraldon y oráculos montan una guardia atenta e inquebrantable sobre el arremolinado portal verde de su base, rechazando a cualquier mortal que ose acercarse sin ser invitado.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Bough Shadow represents sacred ground for druids, housing one of the tangible thresholds linking Azeroth directly to the domain of the Green Flight and the Emerald Dream.",["race:NightElf"]="Lying deep beyond the ruins of Forest Song, this great tree was shaped by kaldorei hands from the branch of Nordrassil itself, standing as a living monument of ancient elven stewardship."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The swirling vortex at the foot of the Great Tree is a direct gateway leading into the Emerald Dream, the untamed spirit realm of Azeroth. It is one of several such natural crossings scattered across the world.",["al"]={"bough shadow portal","what is the portal in bough shadow","green portal ashenvale"},["q"]="What is the glowing green portal here?"},{["a"]="Ysera's Green Dragonflight is charged with watching over the Emerald Dream and its direct passages into the physical world. Emerald drakes and dragonspawn patrol Bough Shadow to ensure no corrupting forces or intruders slip through the threshold.",["al"]={"why are there dragons in ashenvale","green dragonflight bough shadow","why green dragons here"},["q"]="Why are green dragons guarding Bough Shadow?"},{["a"]="The tree was planted millennia ago by night elf druids loyal to Fandral Staghelm, who used a cutting taken from the boughs of the World Tree, Nordrassil, to root over the site.",["al"]={"who made bough shadow","who planted the tree","tree origin bough shadow"},["q"]="Who planted the Great Tree here?"},{["a"]="No. The gateway remains tightly sealed to mortals in the physical world, and venturing too close will provoke the wrath of the surrounding elite dragonkin guards.",["al"]={"can i go through the portal","enter bough shadow portal","how to enter dream portal"},["q"]="Can players enter the portal?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","bough shadow","dragonspawn","dreamstalker","emerald dream","great tree","green dragons","phantim","portal"},["n"]="Bough Shadow",["s"]="Bough Shadow is a secluded grove tucked away in the far northeastern corner of Ashenvale, east of Forest Song. It centers around a colossal Great Tree rooted over an ancient portal leading directly into the Emerald Dream.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Bough Shadow houses one of the rare Great Trees grown from a cutting of the World Tree, Nordrassil. Planted long ago by druids following Fandral Staghelm, its roots plunge deep into the earth around a natural crossing into the Emerald Dream. Today, the tranquil yet imposing grove is heavily guarded by the Green Dragonflight. Emerald drakes such as Phantim and Dreamstalker circle above the canopy, while patrols of Emeraldon dragonspawn and oracles keep a vigilant, unyielding watch over the swirling green portal at its base, turning away any mortal who approaches unbidden.",["t"]="A Gateway to the Dream"}}}}}
t["subzone:boulder-lode-mine"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,247,15.464.0,19.338.0,31.159.0,39.200.0,53.201.0,56.212.0",["h"]="e752a6",["n"]="Mina Pedrusco",["s"]="Mina Pedrusco. Mina Pedrusco es una agresiva excavación excavada en las colinas del noreste de Los Baldíos. Aunque los estandartes orcos y las torres de vigilancia sugieren que la Horda estableció primero el lugar, ahora está firmemente tomada y explotada por la despiadada Ventura y Cía. La presencia de arquitectura orca desgastada alrededor de la entrada de Mina Pedrusco indica que la Horda en su momento poseyó o fundó el yacimiento. Hoy en día, sin embargo, la zona está plagada de capataces y matones de Ventura y Cía. que trabajan bajo las órdenes de Boss Copperplug. La organización goblin explota a cielo abierto el cañón sin apenas consideración por el ecosistema local o sus trabajadores, motivado únicamente por la búsqueda de minerales valiosos, gemas de alto rendimiento y maquinaria industrial.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Seeing the Venture Company operating out of fortifications marked with Horde standards is an irritating reminder of how aggressively the goblin cartel encroaches on Kalimdor lands.",["profession:Mining"]="The deep excavation tunnels cut straight into the arid hills, revealing rich mineral veins that the Venture Company mercilessly strips."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The mine is operated by the Venture Company under the immediate authority of Boss Copperplug, guarded by heavily armed corporate enforcers and labor overseers.",["al"]={"who runs boulder lode mine","boulder lode boss","who is in boulder lode"},["q"]="Who controls Boulder Lode Mine?"},{["a"]="The surviving orcish woodwork, watchtowers, and weathered Horde banners strongly indicate that the Horde initially established or claimed the site before the Venture Company moved in and took control.",["al"]={"orc banners at boulder lode","horde mine","why are there horde flags"},["q"]="Did the Horde originally own this mine?"},{["a"]="Dizzywig caught wind that a miner inside Boulder Lode dug up an unusually large and valuable emerald, and he hires cutthroat freelancers to infiltrate the tunnels and swipe it for a cut of the profits.",["al"]={"dizzywig mine quest","emerald quest barrens","miners fortune"},["q"]="Why is Wharfmaster Dizzywig interested in this place?"},{["a"]="Boss Copperplug possesses the essential operating manual for the mysterious samophlange machinery found nearby, and engineers in Ratchet send adventurers to recover the book and its scattered pages from his crew.",["al"]={"samophlange manual boulder lode","copperplug manual","rilli greasygob mine"},["q"]="What is Boss Copperplug's connection to the samophlange?"}},["kw"]={"boss copperplug","boulder lode mine","dizzywig","miner's fortune","samophlange manual","the barrens","venture company"},["n"]="Boulder Lode Mine",["s"]="Boulder Lode Mine is an aggressive excavation cut into the hills of the northeastern Barrens. Though orcish banners and watchtowers suggest the Horde first established the site, it is now firmly seized and operated by the ruthless Venture Company.",["sec"]={{["b"]="The presence of weathered orcish architecture around the mouth of Boulder Lode Mine indicates that the Horde once held or founded the claim. Today, however, the area crawls with Venture Company overseers and enforcers working under the direction of Boss Copperplug. The goblin syndicate strip-mines the canyon with little regard for the local ecosystem or their workers, driven purely by the search for valuable minerals, high-yield gems, and industrial machinery.",["t"]="Corporate Claim"},{["b"]="Word of the riches pulled from Boulder Lode Mine has reached outside ears in Ratchet. Wharfmaster Dizzywig has dispatched mercenaries to pocket a rumored massive emerald unearthed in its tunnels, while engineers seeking to understand complex goblin machinery know Boss Copperplug keeps key operational manuals hidden away within his camp.",["t"]="Gems and Schematics"}}}}}
t["subzone:boulderslide-cavern"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,271,16.421.0,20.353.1,33.236.0,16.188.0,37.176.0,43.185.0",["h"]="e5d00e",["n"]="Cueva del Alud",["s"]="Cueva del Alud. La Cueva del Alud es una madriguera subterránea escondida en el extremo más profundo del Barranco del Alud, en Sierra Espolón. Sirve como guarida principal y lugar de excavación para los kóbold Alud locales, que excavan túneles de forma obsesiva en busca de formaciones minerales brillantes. Los kóbold Alud han horadado las profundidades de los riscos de Sierra Espolón, estableciendo la Cueva del Alud como su fortaleza. A diferencia de las alimañas ordinarias que solo buscan cobijo, estos kóbold extraen frenéticamente resonita, un raro cristal morado brillante incrustado por toda la piedra. Los cristales pulsan con una magia terránea residual, lo que sume a las criaturas en un frenesí defensivo contra cualquier intruso que se acerque a su excavación.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="The resonite crystals and the slumbering earthen Goggeroc both resonate with primordial earth magic, an echo of the world's ancient stone shapers.",["profession:Mining"]="The cavern is intensely worked by the Boulderslide clan, who tunnel relentlessly to uncover glowing veins of magical resonite."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The kobolds are mining resonite, a rare purple crystal found embedded in the cavern's rock walls. The mineral hums with faint traces of earthen magic, making it a valuable prize and causing the kobolds to guard their caches fanatically.",["al"]={"what is resonite","purple crystals stonetalon","why are kobolds mining"},["q"]="What are the kobolds mining here?"},{["a"]="Goggeroc is an ancient earthen who lies dormant within a resonite cask deep inside the cavern. The kobolds' excavation around his resting place risks disturbing his centuries-long slumber.",["al"]={"goggeroc lore","earthen in boulderslide","sleeping giant in cave"},["q"]="Who is Goggeroc?"},{["a"]="The cavern entrance sits at the far end of Boulderslide Ravine, nestled in the craggy mountains of southern Stonetalon Mountains, just northeast of the path toward the Barrens.",["al"]={"boulderslide cavern location","how to find boulderslide cavern","where is the cave"},["q"]="Where is Boulderslide Cavern located?"},{["a"]="The Horde keeps watch on the cavern to curb the aggressive kobold infestation spilling into the ravine, and out of interest in the magical properties of the resonite crystals they mine.",["al"]={"horde quests boulderslide","why send me to boulderslide"},["q"]="Why is the Horde interested in this cavern?"}},["kw"]={"boulderslide","cavern","earthen","goggeroc","kobold","resonite","stonetalon"},["n"]="Boulderslide Cavern",["s"]="Boulderslide Cavern is a subterranean warren tucked at the deepest end of Boulderslide Ravine in the Stonetalon Mountains. It serves as the primary den and excavation site for the local Boulderslide kobolds, who obsessively tunnel in search of glowing mineral formations.",["sec"]={{["b"]="The Boulderslide kobolds have burrowed deep into the crags of Stonetalon, establishing Boulderslide Cavern as their stronghold. Unlike ordinary vermin merely seeking shelter, these kobolds mine frantically for resonite, a rare glowing purple crystal embedded throughout the stone. The crystals pulse with lingering earthen magic, driving the creatures into a defensive frenzy against any intruders who approach their dig.",["t"]="The Resonite Dig"},{["b"]="Deeper inside the caverns, reckless excavation has breached ancient secrets. Embedded in the subterranean rock lies a resonite cask containing Goggeroc, a slumbering earthen from ages past. The kobolds' relentless digging around this mystical relic risks awakening a being imbued with primordial stone magic, posing a sudden danger to the entire ravine.",["t"]="The Slumbering Giant"}}}}}
t["subzone:boulderslide-ravine"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,306,21.567.0,19.442.0,37.130.0,43.128.0,59.222.0,39.172.0",["h"]="32a91c",["n"]="Barranco del Alud",["s"]="Barranco del Alud. El Barranco del Alud es un cañón escarpado y apartado escondido en los picos centrales de Sierra Espolón, al que se accede a través de la Senda de las Tejedoras. En gran medida a salvo de los enfrentamientos directos entre la Horda y la Alianza, sirve como aproximación rocosa a la Cueva del Alud y sigue siendo el hogar de bestias salvajes de la montaña. Escondido junto a la Senda de las Tejedoras, el Barranco del Alud es un estrecho corte en la roca en las alturas de Sierra Espolón. Mientras los leñadores, los elfos de la noche y la Horda luchan por la madera y los claros sagrados por toda la región, este paso risco permanece relativamente libre de fuerzas militares. Carneros salvajes de montaña y bestias de los riscos que merodean como los Cliff Stormers componen la fauna local, recorriendo las traicioneras cornisas y las escarpadas paredes de piedra. Los prospectores también vigilan el barranco, ya que con frecuencia afloran ricas vetas de mineral a lo largo de las laderas rocosas que conducen hacia la red de cavernas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Mining"]="The steep rock walls of the ravine are a reliable place to spot mineral veins exposed by the mountain's shifting stone.",["race:Tauren"]="The faded art inside the small side cave bears the distinct touch of tauren tribal markers, hinting at ancestral paths through the Stonetalon heights."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Boulderslide Ravine is located in the Stonetalon Mountains. It is reached by traveling along Webwinder Path into the higher crags.",["al"]={"boulderslide ravine location","how to get to boulderslide ravine","where is boulderslide ravine"},["q"]="Where is Boulderslide Ravine located?"},{["a"]="The ravine is mainly populated by local wildlife, particularly mountain rams and dangerous crag stalkers such as Cliff Stormers.",["al"]={"boulderslide ravine mobs","what is in boulderslide ravine"},["q"]="What creatures inhabit Boulderslide Ravine?"},{["a"]="Facing the cavern entrance is a small alcove lit by torches and stocked with old barrels. Its stone walls display tribal pictographs that resemble traditional tauren art, pointing to past use by local wanderers or hunters.",["al"]={"abandoned cave boulderslide","cave in boulderslide ravine","tauren cave stonetalon"},["q"]="What is the abandoned cave across from Boulderslide Cavern?"},{["a"]="It serves as the natural approach to Boulderslide Cavern, a subterranean lair deep in the mountains, and offers valuable mineral outcroppings for travelers passing through.",["al"]={"what is boulderslide ravine for","boulderslide ravine purpose"},["q"]="Why is Boulderslide Ravine significant?"}},["kw"]={"boulderslide cavern","boulderslide ravine","cliff stormer","rams","stonetalon","webwinder path"},["n"]="Boulderslide Ravine",["s"]="Boulderslide Ravine is a rugged, secluded canyon tucked away in the central peaks of the Stonetalon Mountains, reached via Webwinder Path. Largely spared from the direct clashes between the Horde and Alliance, it serves as the rocky approach to Boulderslide Cavern and remains home to wild mountain beasts.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away off Webwinder Path, Boulderslide Ravine is a narrow cut of rock in the Stonetalon heights. While loggers, night elves, and the Horde battle over timber and sacred glades throughout the region, this craggy pass remains relatively undisturbed by military forces. Wild mountain rams and roaming crag beasts like Cliff Stormers make up the local fauna, navigating the treacherous ledges and sheer stone walls. Prospectors also keep an eye on the ravine, as rich mineral veins frequently crop up along the rocky slopes leading deeper toward the cavern network.",["t"]="A Quiet Mountain Pass"},{["b"]="Opposite the entrance to Boulderslide Cavern lies a small, quiet cave overlooking the ravine. Lit by rough torches and stacked with weathered supply barrels, the shelter contains primitive tribal paintings across its interior walls. The crude artwork bears a striking resemblance to ancient tauren designs, suggesting that native tribes traveled or sought temporary shelter in these crags long before modern conflict swept into the mountains.",["t"]="Traces in the Stone"}}}}}
t["subzone:brackwell-pumpkin-patch"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="23,317,14.602.0,19.504.1,38.236.0,46.283.0,16.221.0,42.276.0",["h"]="e944ef",["n"]="Plantación de Calabazas de Brackwell",["s"]="Plantación de Calabazas de Brackwell. La Plantación de Calabazas de Brackwell es una granja invadida en el sureste del Bosque de Elwynn. Antaño hogar de la familia Brackwell, los campos y la cabaña han sido tomados por completo por la Hermandad Defias como escondite operativo. Sirve de punto de encuentro para pícaros conspiradores y base de operaciones para el contrabando de oro robado. Situada al sureste del hogar de los Stonefield, la granja de los Brackwell fue en su día una productiva parcela de labranza en Elwynn. Hoy en día, los legítimos propietarios han desaparecido sin dejar rastro, expulsados o algo peor a causa de la creciente marea criminal. En su ausencia, la Hermandad Defias se adueñó de la robusta cabaña y los campos abandonados de la granja. La zona funciona como refugio y puesto de transferencia, donde los forajidos se reagrupan lejos de la atenta mirada de las patrullas de Villadorada. Conspiradores de alto perfil como Morgan el Coleccionista utilizan la aislada parcela para recibir cargamentos de oro obtenido ilícitamente y sustraído de las minas del bosque.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warlock"]="The farm's shack shelters the fugitive apprentice Surena Caledon, whose stolen bloodstone choker is needed to bind a voidwalker.",["faction:Alliance"]="The overrun patch marks one of the easternmost operational bases of the Defias inside Elwynn, directly threatening nearby farms and trade routes."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Their exact fate remains unknown. When the Defias Brotherhood expanded their presence throughout southeastern Elwynn Forest, the Brackwells were either forced to flee or killed, leaving their pumpkin fields and farmhouse to the bandits.",["al"]={"where are the brackwells","who lived at brackwell farm","brackwell family fate"},["q"]="What happened to the Brackwell family?"},{["a"]="The farm provides an out-of-the-way base close to the forest's borders. It allows the brotherhood to store plundered goods and coordinate smuggling operations, such as receiving shipments of stolen mine gold via couriers like Morgan the Collector, well away from the Stormwind Guard.",["al"]={"why are defias here","what are bandits doing at the pumpkin patch","defias at brackwell"},["q"]="Why is the Defias Brotherhood using this farm?"},{["a"]="Princess is an enormous, prize-winning pig originally raised by the Brackwells. Left behind when the farm fell, she has grown even larger by regularly breaking into the nearby Stonefield Farm to devour their prized crops.",["al"]={"giant pig","princess pig","why is there a huge boar here"},["q"]="Who is Princess?"},{["a"]="Surena Caledon, an apprentice of the Stormwind warlock trainer Gakin the Darkbinder, stole a powerful bloodstone choker and fled to the farm to hide alongside her lover, the Defias bandit Erlan Drudgemoor. Gakin sends novice warlocks here to execute her and recover the relic.",["al"]={"warlock quest brackwell","surena caledon","gakin voidwalker quest"},["q"]="Why do warlocks come to the pumpkin patch?"}},["kw"]={"brackwell","defias","elwynn","erlan drudgemoor","morgan the collector","princess","pumpkin patch","surena caledon"},["n"]="Brackwell Pumpkin Patch",["s"]="Brackwell Pumpkin Patch is an overrun farmstead in southeastern Elwynn Forest. Once home to the Brackwell family, the fields and cottage have been thoroughly seized by the Defias Brotherhood as an operational hideout. It serves as a meeting point for rogue conspirators and a staging ground for smuggling stolen gold.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated southeast of the Stonefield homestead, the Brackwell farm was once a productive patch of Elwynn farmland. Today, the rightful owners have vanished without a trace, driven out or worse by the rising criminal tide. In their absence, the Defias Brotherhood claimed the farm's sturdy cottage and overgrown fields. The area functions as a safehouse and transfer post, where brigands regroup away from the watchful eyes of Goldshire's patrols. High-profile conspirators like Morgan the Collector use the isolated patch to receive shipments of illicitly gathered gold skimmed from the forest's mines.",["t"]="A Bandit Haven"},{["b"]="The Defias are not the only troublemakers prowling the pumpkin vines. The Brackwells left behind an enormous prize-winning sow named Princess, who roams the patch and constantly terrorizes neighboring fields. Meanwhile, the farmhouse attic and outbuildings shelter dangerous personal dealings: bandit Erlan Drudgemoor seduced Surena Caledon, a rogue warlock apprentice who fled her master in Stormwind with a stolen bloodstone artifact, bringing the attention of dark practitioners down upon the hideout.",["t"]="Pigs and Dark Magic"}}}}}
t["subzone:brambleblade-ravine"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,341,26.544.0,28.181.0,53.214.0,46.147.0,41.199.0",["h"]="938667",["n"]="Barranco Cortazarza",["s"]="Barranco Cortazarza. El Barranco Cortazarza es un cañón escarpado que se abre paso en el extremo nororiental de la Mesa de la Nube Roja. Sirve como guarida fortificada para la tribu de jabaespines Erizaclara, quienes asaltan persistentemente el cercano asentamiento tauren de Campamento Narache. Los jóvenes valientes tauren son enviados aquí para demostrar su fuerza y proteger su tierra natal de estos fieros intrusos. Esculpido en la tierra abrasada por el sol de la Mesa de la Nube Roja, el Barranco Cortazarza está repleto de densas zarzas espinosas y campamentos de jabaespines. La tribu Erizaclara utiliza esta fortaleza natural como base de operaciones para sus asaltos contra Campamento Narache, amenazando la seguridad de los jóvenes tauren que alcanzan la edad adulta. Los chamanes y guerreros Erizaclara, liderados por el jefe Cornapunta Mantospina, habitan en las profundidades del barranco entre jabatos de combate entrenados. Para los Shu'halo, adentrarse en el corazón del cañón es un rito de iniciación crucial y una sombría necesidad para asegurar las llanuras.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Clearing out the aggressive Bristlebacks in Brambleblade Ravine helps solidify the Horde's early foothold across Mulgore.",["race:Tauren"]="For young tauren coming of age at Camp Narache, striking into Brambleblade Ravine is one of the very first tests of martial and spiritual endurance to defend the tribe."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Brambleblade Ravine is a canyon situated on the northeastern edge of Red Cloud Mesa in Mulgore. It is heavily inhabited by Bristleback quilboar and serves as their local stronghold.",["al"]={"brambleblade ravine","what is brambleblade ravine","brambleblade mulgore"},["q"]="What is Brambleblade Ravine?"},{["a"]="The Bristlebacks are fiercely territorial and view the presence of the tauren as an encroachment upon lands they claim. From Brambleblade Ravine, they launch frequent raids on the nearby settlement of Camp Narache.",["al"]={"why quilboar attacking","bristleback motives","quilboar camp narache"},["q"]="Why are the Bristleback quilboar attacking from here?"},{["a"]="The quilboar here are led by Chief Sharptusk Thornmantle, a formidable chieftain who resides in a large hut located towards the back of the ravine.",["al"]={"brambleblade leader","quilboar boss mulgore","chief sharptusk thornmantle"},["q"]="Who leads the quilboar in Brambleblade Ravine?"},{["a"]="Tauren elders and chieftains at Camp Narache task fledgling braves with entering the ravine to push back the Bristleback threat, cull their numbers, and defeat their leadership to keep the mesa safe.",["al"]={"tauren quests brambleblade","why go to brambleblade","camp narache quests"},["q"]="Why do young tauren travel to the ravine?"}},["kw"]={"brambleblade","bristleback","camp narache","mulgore","quilboar","ravine","red cloud mesa","thornmantle"},["n"]="Brambleblade Ravine",["s"]="Brambleblade Ravine is a rugged canyon cutting into the northeastern edge of Red Cloud Mesa. It serves as a fortified den for the Bristleback quilboar tribe, who persistently raid the nearby tauren settlement of Camp Narache. Young tauren braves are sent here to prove their strength and protect their homeland from these fierce interlopers.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Carved into the sun-scorched earth of Red Cloud Mesa, Brambleblade Ravine is choked with dense, thorny briars and quilboar encampments. The Bristleback tribe uses this natural fortress as a staging ground for raids against Camp Narache, threatening the safety of young tauren coming of age. Bristleback shamans and warriors, led by Chief Sharptusk Thornmantle, dwell deep within the ravine among trained battleboars. For the Shu'halo, striking into the heart of the canyon is a crucial rite of passage and a grim necessity to secure the plains.",["t"]="A Thorn in the Mesa's Side"}}}}}
t["subzone:bramblescar"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,238,17.466.0,17.402.0,25.164.0,46.184.0,29.121.0,43.157.0",["h"]="bf879a",["n"]="Rajazarza",["s"]="Rajazarza. Rajazarza es un asentamiento de jabaespines Crinfilada fuertemente fortificado, situado en el sur de Los Baldíos. Espesas zarzas espinosas protegen el campamento mientras sus habitantes libran una brutal guerra contra la tribu rival Erizapúa al otro lado del Camino del Oro. Esculpido entre los gigantescos y escarpados zarzales del sur de Los Baldíos, Rajazarza sirve como un reducto vital para los jabaespines Crinfilada. Estas zarzas defensivas crecen lo bastante densas y afiladas como para disuadir a los viajeros ocasionales, pero los jabaespines de su interior distan mucho de ser pacíficos. Ferozmente territoriales y hostiles con los forasteros, entablan constantes escaramuzas contra cualquiera que se aventure cerca de sus fronteras, pues consideran a todo aquel que no sea jabaespín un intruso en tierras bendecidas por sus antiguos dioses jabalí.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Securing the Gold Road against quillboar raids from Bramblescar is crucial to maintaining safe passage between Crossroads, Camp Taurajo, and the southern frontier."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Bramblescar is inhabited by the Razormane tribe of quilboar, who defend their thorn-choked encampment against both rival quilboar and any travelers passing through.",["al"]={"who is here","bramblescar mobs","bramblescar quilboar"},["q"]="Who lives in Bramblescar?"},{["a"]="The Razormane of Bramblescar and the Bristleback quilboar across the road at Agama'gor are bitter enemies locked in a fierce territorial blood feud for control of the southern Barrens.",["al"]={"why are they at war","razormane vs bristleback","quilboar war"},["q"]="Why are the quilboar here fighting each other?"},{["a"]="Bramblescar lies in the southern plains of the Barrens, positioned just east of the main Gold Road across from Agama'gor.",["al"]={"bramblescar location","where is bramblescar","how to find bramblescar"},["q"]="Where is Bramblescar located?"},{["a"]="Yes. The Razormane quilboar view the Horde as invaders who have encroached on their sacred tribal lands, and they will attack any traveler who wanders close.",["al"]={"is bramblescar friendly","horde reputation bramblescar"},["q"]="Are the quilboar here hostile to the Horde?"}},["kw"]={"agama'gor","barrens","bramblescar","bristleback","gold road","quilboar","razormane"},["n"]="Bramblescar",["s"]="Bramblescar is a heavily fortified Razormane quilboar settlement situated in the southern Barrens. Thick, thorny brambles shield the encampment as its inhabitants wage a brutal war against the rival Bristleback tribe across the Gold Road.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Carved into the jagged, giant briars of the southern Barrens, Bramblescar serves as a vital redoubt for the Razormane quilboar. These defensive brambles grow thick and sharp enough to deter casual wanderers, but the quilboar within are far from peaceful. Fiercely territorial and hostile to outsiders, they mount continuous skirmishes against anyone who ventures near their borders, viewing all non-quilboar as intruders upon land blessed by their ancient boar gods.",["t"]="A Thorned Redoubt"},{["b"]="Bramblescar sits in perpetual tension directly across the Gold Road from Agama'gor, an encampment held by the rival Bristleback tribe. The two factions are locked in an unrelenting tribal war for dominion over the southern Barrens. Between fighting off Horde travelers along the highway and repelling Bristleback raiding parties, the Razormane warriors of Bramblescar remain on constant, violent alert.",["t"]="Tribal Blood Feud"}}}}}
t["subzone:brewnall-village"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,380,27.637.0,25.243.0,53.234.0,57.266.0,36.244.0",["h"]="849118",["n"]="Las Birras",["s"]="Las Birras. Las Birras es un pequeño asentamiento enano ubicado en el Valle Escalofrío, cerca de la entrada a Gnomeregan. Establecido por la familia Barleybrew, este puesto avanzado sirve como campo de pruebas para audaces experimentos cerveceros y como defensa regional frente a las bestias salvajes. A pesar de llamarse aldea, funciona principalmente como un rústico campamento en las nevadas tierras bajas gnomísticas de Dun Morogh. Resguardada entre los ventisqueros del Valle Escalofrío, Las Birras se encuentra de lleno en los dominios tradicionalmente gnomos del oeste de Dun Morogh. El asentamiento es el hogar del clan Barleybrew, unos incondicionales maestros cerveceros enanos dedicados a perfeccionar recetas ancestrales y elaborar la cerveza negra definitiva. Aunque se la califica de aldea, el puesto avanzado consta en su mayoría de tiendas de campaña y equipo de destilación al aire libre en vez de arquitectura permanente de piedra. Entre probar lotes experimentales de cerveza y defenderse de los feroces lobos y osos de la zona, los Barleybrew dependen en gran medida de los montañeros itinerantes para reunir ingredientes raros y mantener seguro el valle.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, the Barleybrews' quest for the ultimate recipe is an honorable pursuit that upholds one of Ironforge's finest traditions.",["race:Gnome"]="Situated close to Gnomeregan, the village is an unexpected dwarven outpost deep within western Dun Morogh's gnomish valleys."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Brewnall Village is a small dwarven camp located in Chill Breeze Valley within western Dun Morogh, just east of Gnomeregan. It serves as an outpost where the Barleybrew clan experiments with new beer recipes and manages local wildlife threats.",["al"]={"where is brewnall","what is brewnall village","brewnall info"},["q"]="What is Brewnall Village?"},{["a"]="Despite carrying the name village, the site is essentially an open-air encampment made up of tents and supply kegs. The Barleybrews have staked out their brewing operation here in the cold climate without building formal stone houses.",["al"]={"why is it a camp","where are the houses","brewnall buildings"},["q"]="Why is it called a village if there are no buildings?"},{["a"]="While the western half of Dun Morogh surrounds Gnomeregan and is primarily inhabited by gnomes, the close alliance between Ironforge and the gnomes makes shared settlement common. The Barleybrews settled here in Chill Breeze Valley to pursue their craft undisturbed.",["al"]={"dwarves near gnomeregan","why are dwarves here","gnome territory dwarf camp"},["q"]="Why is a dwarven settlement located in gnomish territory?"},{["a"]="The encampment faces frequent attacks from the valley's aggressive wildlife, particularly crag boars, bears, and frost wolves. Additionally, the Barleybrews are constantly searching for rare and exotic ingredients to invent new, superior brews.",["al"]={"brewnall quests","what do the barleybrews need","village problems"},["q"]="What problems do the residents face?"}},["kw"]={"barleybrew","beer","brewnall","chill breeze valley","dun morogh","gnomeregan","stout"},["n"]="Brewnall Village",["s"]="Brewnall Village is a small dwarven settlement nestled in Chill Breeze Valley near the entrance to Gnomeregan. Established by the Barleybrew family, this outpost serves as a proving ground for bold brewing experiments and regional defense against wild beasts. Despite being called a village, it functions largely as a rustic encampment in the snowy gnomish lowlands of Dun Morogh.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away in the snowdrifts of Chill Breeze Valley, Brewnall Village lies squarely within the traditional gnomish reaches of western Dun Morogh. The settlement is home to the Barleybrew clan, stalwart dwarven brewers devoted to perfecting age-old recipes and crafting the ultimate stout. Though dubbed a village, the outpost consists mostly of tents and outdoor brewing equipment rather than permanent stone architecture. Between testing experimental batches of ale and defending against the ferocious local wolves and bears, the Barleybrews rely heavily on wandering mountaineers to gather rare ingredients and keep the valley secure.",["t"]="A Bitter Brew in the Valley"}}}}}
t["subzone:brightwood-grove"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,279,17.516.0,26.111.0,40.174.0,40.207.0,48.152.0",["h"]="895626",["n"]="Arboleda del Destello",["s"]="Arboleda del Destello. Arboleda del Destello es una sombría extensión de bosque situada justo al oeste de Villa Oscura, en Bosque del Ocaso. En su día formó parte del sereno paisaje agrícola de la región, pero ahora está infestada de salvajes huargen Nocturnos que acampan entre granjas en ruinas y atacan a cualquier viajero que se acerque demasiado. Situada a la vista del perímetro de Villa Oscura, Arboleda del Destello representa el peligro insidioso que amenaza las fronteras del pueblo. Las granjas y cercas que antaño delimitaban apacibles tierras de cultivo yacen ahora derruidas y podridas. En su lugar, los huargen Nocturnos han levantado toscos campamentos y merodean por los claros cubiertos de maleza. La proximidad de estas bestias lupinas plantea una amenaza constante para la villa, obligando a la Guardia Nocturna y a los aventureros de paso a diezmar continuamente su número antes de que el asentamiento sea invadido.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="The dark thickets of the grove provide harsh terrain for tracking the vicious Nightbane, testing any hunter's awareness against ambushes lurking behind the tree line.",["faction:Alliance"]="Brightwood Grove sits right outside the gates of Darkshire, making the elimination of its worgen packs vital to keeping the beleaguered town from being cut off from the west."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Brightwood Grove is located in eastern Duskwood, lying just west of the town of Darkshire along the main paths.",["al"]={"brightwood grove location","where is brightwood grove","brightwood duskwood"},["q"]="Where is Brightwood Grove?"},{["a"]="The grove is heavily infested by savage Nightbane worgen. These cursed wolf-men have established crude camps throughout the ruined buildings and attack anyone who approaches.",["al"]={"monsters in brightwood grove","brightwood enemies","what lives in brightwood"},["q"]="What creatures inhabit Brightwood Grove?"},{["a"]="Because Brightwood Grove sits immediately west of Darkshire, the aggressive worgen packs lurking in the brush are an immediate hazard to town patrols, supply lines, and any travelers arriving along the road.",["al"]={"why is brightwood grove dangerous","darkshire brightwood threat"},["q"]="Why is the grove dangerous to Darkshire?"},{["a"]="No. The few stone buildings and farmsteads on the outskirts of the grove lie entirely in ruins, abandoned to the elements and occupied by roving worgen.",["al"]={"is anyone friendly in brightwood","brightwood town"},["q"]="Are there any friendly settlements in the grove?"}},["kw"]={"brightwood grove","darkshire","duskwood","night watch","nightbane","wolf men","worgen"},["n"]="Brightwood Grove",["s"]="Brightwood Grove is a shadowed expanse of woodland located just west of Darkshire in Duskwood. Once part of the region's serene agrarian landscape, it is now infested with savage Nightbane worgen who make camp among ruined homesteads and attack any travelers wandering too close.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated within sight of Darkshire's perimeter, Brightwood Grove represents the creeping peril threatening the town's borders. The homesteads and fences that once demarcated peaceful farmland now lie collapsed and rotting. In their place, crude camps have been erected by the Nightbane worgen, who prowl the overgrown clearings. The proximity of these wolf-beasts poses an ongoing threat to the town, forcing the Night Watch and passing adventurers to continually cull their numbers before the settlement is overrun.",["t"]="A Grove in Shadow"}}}}}
t["subzone:brill"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="5,273,29.744.0,32.429.0,16.135.0,52.252.0,37.176.0,54.164.0",["h"]="721854",["n"]="Rémol",["s"]="Rémol. Rémol es el principal asentamiento de los Renegados en el corazón de los Claros de Tirisfal, situado justo al norte de las Ruinas de Lordaeron. Antaño una próspera villa humana, hoy sirve como centro administrativo y militar para los no-muertos recién despertados que se aventuran más allá de los confines de Camposanto. Antes de la Tercera Guerra, Rémol era una animada aldea bajo la influencia de nobles regionales como las familias Barov y Agamand. Esa prosperidad terminó cuando Kel'Thuzad eligió la zona para los primeros experimentos del Culto de los Malditos con la peste de la no-muerte. La devastadora plaga se extendió con tal rapidez entre la población que las milicias locales fueron expulsadas, dejando a su paso un inmenso cementerio. Reconstruido ahora por los Renegados bajo el liderazgo del Magistrado Sevren, el pueblo conserva su desgastada arquitectura de Lordaeron bajo una atmósfera de sombrío propósito. Rémol funciona como centro de mando regional, coordinando las defensas frente a las incursiones de la Cruzada Escarlata, los restos errantes de la Plaga y las bestias autóctonas deformadas por la corrupción nigromántica.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="The zeppelin dock outside town serves as the northern Horde's primary link between Lordaeron and allied strongholds in Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms.",["race:Undead"]="For Forsaken venturing out from Deathknell, Brill is the first glimpse of civilization and the starting ground for proving loyalty to the Dark Lady."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Magistrate Sevren oversees the civil administration and local defenses of Brill on behalf of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken.",["al"]={"brill leader","who is in charge of brill","magistrate of brill"},["q"]="Who rules Brill?"},{["a"]="Kel'Thuzad conducted some of his very first live experiments with the Plague of Undeath in Brill. The contagion wiped out the local human population with horrifying speed, necessitating a mass graveyard to inter the victims before they rose as Scourge.",["al"]={"brill graveyard","cemetery near brill","why so many graves"},["q"]="Why is there such a massive graveyard outside Brill?"},{["a"]="Aside from lodging weary travelers, the tavern's cellar serves as a base for apothecaries conducting chemical and toxicological experiments on captured Scarlet Crusade zealots.",["al"]={"gallows end","brill inn","what is happening in the brill tavern"},["q"]="What is Gallows' End Tavern used for?"},{["a"]="The zeppelin tower operated by goblin crews connects Lordaeron directly to Kalimdor outside Orgrimmar, as well as south to Grom'gol Base Camp in Stranglethorn Vale.",["al"]={"brill zeppelin destinations","where do blimps go brill","brill flight paths"},["q"]="Where does the zeppelin tower outside Brill travel to?"}},["kw"]={"brill","forsaken","gallows end","lordaeron","magistrate sevren","tirisfal glades","zeppelin"},["n"]="Brill",["s"]="Brill is the primary Forsaken settlement in the heart of Tirisfal Glades, situated just north of the Ruins of Lordaeron. Once a prosperous human town, it now serves as the administrative and military hub for newly awakened undead stepping beyond the confines of Deathknell.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the Third War, Brill was a lively village under the sway of regional nobles such as the Barov and Agamand families. That prosperity ended when Kel'Thuzad chose the area for the Cult of the Damned's earliest experiments with the Plague of Undeath. The devastating blight swept through the population so quickly that local militia were driven out, leaving a sprawling mass graveyard in its wake.\010\010Now rebuilt by the Forsaken under the leadership of Magistrate Sevren, the town retains its weathered Lordaeron architecture beneath an atmosphere of grim purpose. Brill functions as the regional command center, coordinating defenses against Scarlet Crusade incursions, roaming Scourge remnants, and native beasts warped by necromantic decay.",["t"]="From Plague Ground to Bastion"},{["b"]="Beyond local defense, Brill is an essential crossroads linking Tirisfal Glades to the wider Horde. Overhead, the goblin-operated zeppelin tower provides transit south toward Durotar and deep into Stranglethorn Vale. Within the settlement, Gallows' End Tavern serves not only as a dark shelter for travelers, but also as a makeshift laboratory where captured Scarlet zealots are interrogated and subjected to apothecarial testing.",["t"]="Crossroads of Northern Lordaeron"}}}}}
t["subzone:brill-town-hall"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,278,26.509.0,37.251.0,22.176.0,49.226.0",["h"]="724f70",["n"]="Concejo de Rémol",["s"]="Concejo de Rémol. El Concejo de Rémol es el núcleo administrativo del asentamiento de Rémol, en el centro de Claros de Tirisfal. Al erigirse como la estructura más prominente del pueblo, sirve como sede cívica desde la que los Renegados gobiernan sus posesiones locales y coordinan la defensa de los claros. Mientras que gran parte de Lordaeron yace destruida y en ruinas, el Concejo de Rémol sigue en pie como un centro cívico funcional bajo el mandato de los no-muertos. En su interior, el Magistrado Sevren dirige los asuntos del pueblo desde su podio, encomendando encargos y directrices vitales a los aventureros renegados. Aparte de la Guarida de los Rapiñadores en las Tierras Altas de Arathi, es uno de los pocos concejos reconocidos en el mundo conocido administrados activamente por los Renegados, sirviendo como una parodia sombría y una continuación funcional de la antigua burocracia municipal de Lordaeron.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Allies of the Horde arriving in Tirisfal can visit the town hall to understand how the Forsaken maintain civil authority and martial order in their darkened homelands.",["race:Undead"]="For Forsaken venturing out from Deathknell, the town hall represents the first taste of structured civic governance under Queen Sylvanas's realm, where local defense and reclamation efforts are formally organized."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It serves as the local seat of government for the settlement of Brill. Forsaken leadership, particularly Magistrate Sevren, uses the building to coordinate local defense, issue decrees, and assign critical tasks to travelers and newly awakened undead.",["al"]={"brill town hall purpose","what is this building","why visit brill town hall"},["q"]="What is the Brill Town Hall used for?"},{["a"]="Magistrate Sevren presides over the town hall from his podium, managing municipal affairs on behalf of the Forsaken and directing operations throughout central Tirisfal Glades.",["al"]={"who runs brill town hall","brill town hall leader","who is the magistrate"},["q"]="Who is in charge here?"},{["a"]="Town halls are typically relics of living human kingdoms. Brill Town Hall is notable for being one of the only active civic halls maintained and operated by the Forsaken, mirroring only places like the Defiler's Den in Arathi.",["al"]={"unique forsaken town hall","are there other forsaken town halls"},["q"]="Why is this town hall notable compared to others?"}},["kw"]={"brill","forsaken","lordaeron","magistrate sevren","sevren","tirisfal glades","town hall"},["n"]="Brill Town Hall",["s"]="Brill Town Hall is the administrative heart of the settlement of Brill in central Tirisfal Glades. Standing as the most prominent structure in town, it serves as the civic headquarters from which the Forsaken govern their local holdings and coordinate the defense of the glades.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While much of Lordaeron lies shattered and ruined, Brill Town Hall remains standing as a functioning civic center under undead rule. Inside, Magistrate Sevren directs town affairs from his podium, handing out vital commissions and directives to Forsaken adventurers. Aside from the Defiler's Den in the Arathi Highlands, it is one of the only recognized town halls in the known world actively run by the Forsaken, serving as a bleak parody and functional continuation of old Lordaeron's municipal bureaucracy.",["t"]="Civic Seat of the Forsaken"}}}}}
t["subzone:burning-blade-coven"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,297,33.554.0,23.490.0,41.117.0,28.118.0,34.127.0,37.216.0",["h"]="08c4f7",["n"]="Aquelarre del Filo Ardiente",["s"]="Aquelarre del Filo Ardiente. Enclavado en los acantilados septentrionales del Valle de los Retos, el Aquelarre del Filo Ardiente es una red de cuevas infestada que amenaza a los nuevos reclutas de la Horda. Cultistas corruptos y demonios invocados acechan en su interior, transformando una antigua caverna de minerales en una base de operaciones para la magia oscura a las puertas de Durotar. Las polvorientas montañas rojas que bordean el Valle de los Retos fueron antaño una mera naturaleza salvaje de prueba para los jóvenes orcos y trols de Lanza Negra que daban sus primeros pasos al servicio de la Horda. En los últimos días, sin embargo, oscuros rituales se han apoderado de las cuevas del norte. Diablillos y engendros menores surgen de la entrada de la caverna, desatando el caos y amenazando a los reclutas. Liderado por el sombrío brujo Yarrog Sombróseo, el culto del Filo Ardiente se ha atrincherado en lo más profundo, convirtiendo lo que solía ser un campo de entrenamiento rutinario en un campo de batalla activo contra la corrupción demoníaca.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warlock"]="The demonic imps and dark rituals here are an early, cautionary glimpse into what happens when fel power is wielded recklessly in open defiance of the Horde.",["race:Orc"]="The presence of the Burning Blade cult so close to the Valley of Trials is an intolerable insult to Thrall's new Horde and a stark reminder of the demon worship the orcs fought to leave behind."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The cave is embedded in the high red rock ridges directly along the northern edge of the Valley of Trials in Durotar.",["al"]={"coven location","where is burning blade coven","valley cave location"},["q"]="Where is the Burning Blade Coven located?"},{["a"]="The coven is led by a warlock named Yarrog Baneshadow, who directs the local rituals and commands the summoned demons.",["al"]={"coven leader","who leads burning blade coven","yarrog"},["q"]="Who leads the cultists here?"},{["a"]="The cave is infested with rogue imps, minor demonic servitors, and mortal acolytes aligned with the shadowy Burning Blade cult.",["al"]={"what mobs are in the cave","coven monsters","demons in valley of trials"},["q"]="What kinds of enemies lurk inside?"},{["a"]="Braving the dark depths of the cave, recovering lost tools like Foreman Thazz'ril's pick, and slaying Yarrog Baneshadow serves as the final initiation rite for new orc and troll adventurers before leaving the valley.",["al"]={"why go to coven","coven purpose","coven final test"},["q"]="Why do new recruits go into the cave?"}},["kw"]={"burning blade coven","demon","durotar","imps","thazz'ril","valley of trials","yarrog baneshadow"},["n"]="Burning Blade Coven",["s"]="Tucked into the northern cliffs of the Valley of Trials, the Burning Blade Coven is an infested cave network threatening the Horde's newest recruits. Corrupted cultists and summoned demons lurk within, turning an old mineral cavern into a staging ground for dark magic right on Durotar's doorstep.",["sec"]={{["b"]="The dusty red mountains rimming the Valley of Trials were once simply a testing wilderness for young orcs and Darkspear trolls taking their first steps in service to the Horde. In recent days, however, dark rituals have taken hold of the northern caves. Imps and lesser fiends spill from the cavern mouth, stirring chaos and threatening recruits. Led by the shadowy warlock Yarrog Baneshadow, the Burning Blade cult has entrenched itself deep inside, turning what was once a routine training ground into an active battleground against demonic corruption.",["t"]="A Shadow Over the Proving Grounds"},{["b"]="Before the demons took root, the caves attracted the attention of local overseers hoping to harvest raw materials for the settlement. Foreman Thazz'ril ventured deep inside on a mineral survey, only to be driven out in haste, leaving valuable equipment behind as the cultists made their presence known. Now, driving back Baneshadow's coven serves as the ultimate proving trial for aspiring warriors, rogues, and spellcasters before they are deemed ready to venture out into greater Durotar.",["t"]="Corruption in the Rocks"}}}}}
t["subzone:calmbreeze-inn"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,286,16.458.0,38.92.0,37.139.0,38.183.0,53.166.0",["h"]="82aa98",["n"]="Posada Brisa Calmada",["s"]="Posada Brisa Calmada. El nombre Posada Brisa Calmada hace referencia a los principales establecimientos que ofrecen cobijo y servicios a lo largo de la Isla de Zephras, situados tanto en Aldea Shen'dar como en Valanaar. Sirven como puntos de descanso esenciales para los viajeros que exploran la isla, albergando instructores de profesiones locales, taberneros y artefactos históricos. Las posadas Brisa Calmada proporcionan un santuario entre los serpenteantes senderos de la Isla de Zephras. En Aldea Shen'dar, la posada funciona bajo la dirección de Coriella Brisa Calmada y hace las veces de núcleo central donde se reúnen los artesanos de la isla, incluidos mentores de herboristería, desuello y encantamiento. Al otro lado, en Valanaar, otra posada Brisa Calmada aloja a los caminantes locales y resguarda curiosidades poco comunes, entre ellas un cristal de audio que registra la historia de la antigua rebelión de Eldre'Thalas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="Miriann Mistblade offers rogue instruction from the hearth of the Shen'dar Village Calmbreeze Inn.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Herbalists visiting Shen'dar Village can seek out Halassa Fernbreeze inside the Calmbreeze Inn to hone their gathering craft."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Calmbreeze Inn locations can be found in both Shen'dar Village and Valaanar on Zephras Isle.",["al"]={"calmbreeze inn location","where is calmbreeze inn","calmbreeze inn map"},["q"]="Where are the Calmbreeze Inns located?"},{["a"]="The Shen'dar Village location is maintained by Innkeeper Coriella Calmbreeze, offering hospitality to island residents and travelers alike.",["al"]={"calmbreeze innkeeper","who runs calmbreeze inn"},["q"]="Who runs the inn in Shen'dar Village?"},{["a"]="In Shen'dar Village, the inn houses Halassa Fernbreeze for Herbalism, Mendalass Tattermend for Skinning, Nasalanna Windsinger for Enchanting, and Miriann Mistblade for Rogue training.",["al"]={"calmbreeze trainers","shen'dar inn trainers"},["q"]="What trainers can be found at the inn?"},{["a"]="Upstairs in the Valaanar inn rests an audio crystal containing Part 3 of 'The Rebellion In Eldre'Thalas', chronicling historic events from the ancient Highborne city.",["al"]={"valaanar audio crystal","the rebellion in eldre'thalas crystal"},["q"]="What is the audio crystal found upstairs in Valaanar?"}},["kw"]={"calmbreeze inn","coriella calmbreeze","eldre'thalas","shen'dar village","valaanar","zephras isle"},["n"]="Calmbreeze Inn",["s"]="Calmbreeze Inn refers to the primary establishments offering shelter and services across Zephras Isle, found in both Shen'dar Village and Valaanar. They serve as essential rest stops for travelers exploring the island, housing local trade trainers, innkeepers, and historical artifacts.",["sec"]={{["b"]="The Calmbreeze Inns provide sanctuary amid the winding trails of Zephras Isle. In Shen'dar Village, the inn operates under Coriella Calmbreeze and doubles as a central hub where island tradesfolk gather, including mentors in herbalism, skinning, and enchanting. Across the way in Valaanar, another Calmbreeze Inn accommodates local wayfarers and shelters rare curios, including an audio crystal recording the history of the ancient rebellion in Eldre'Thalas.",["t"]="Rest on the Isle"}}}}}
t["subzone:camp-narache"] = {["faq"]={{["a"]="El Campamento Narache es la aldea de inicio para los jóvenes tauren, situada en lo alto de la Mesa de la Nube Roja, en el sur de Mulgore. Es el campamento central de la tribu Vientaguilar y sirve como santuario donde cazadores, guerreros, druidas y chamanes novatos dominan sus artes antes de viajar hacia el Poblado Pezuña de Sangre y Cima del Trueno.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="fc3024",["i"]=1,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="El Jefe Vientaguilar guía a los valientes de la tribu y coordina las defensas de la mesa, junto a la venerada anciana de la tribu, la Gran Madre Vientaguilar. Los instructores y ancianos de la tribu se reúnen en el centro del campamento para instruir a los jóvenes aventureros.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="7a77b2",["i"]=2,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="El campamento es hostigado continuamente por los jabaespines Erizacongelada que operan desde el Barranco Cortazarza, al este. Además de los jabalíes de batalla salvajes y los zancudos que deambulan por los riscos cercanos, el persistente peligro de las bandas de centauros depredadores mantiene a los valientes Vientaguilar en alerta constante.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="45d14a",["i"]=3,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="La Mesa de la Nube Roja está delimitada de forma natural por escarpados acantilados. La única forma de bajar a las grandes llanuras de Mulgore es a través de un sendero de montaña custodiado que se dirige hacia el norte, vigilado por los valientes Vientaguilar para evitar que las bestias hostiles y los jabaespines tiendan emboscadas a los viajeros.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="3376c5",["i"]=4,["q"]="",["sp"]=0}},["fp"]="12,358,27.590.0,29.487.0,21.318.0,22.237.0,32.285.0,36.250.0",["h"]="1bf792",["n"]="Campamento Narache",["s"]="Campamento Narache. El Campamento Narache es una aldea aislada situada en la Mesa de la Nube Roja, en el sur de Mulgore. Sirve como hogar ancestral de la tribu Vientaguilar y como terreno de pruebas donde los jóvenes tauren comienzan su entrenamiento. Protegido muy por encima de las llanuras, el campamento mantiene tradiciones ancestrales mientras se defiende constantemente del avance de los jabaespines y de las persistentes amenazas de los centauros. Situado en el extremo norte de la elevada Mesa de la Nube Roja, el Campamento Narache es el asentamiento principal de la tribu Vientaguilar. La aldea consta de varias tiendas y pabellones grandes de piel, incluida una tienda comunal para los valientes heridos, una armería, una tienda de panadería y una sala de los espíritus dedicada a la meditación y a la comunión ancestral. En el centro del campamento, los ancianos de la tribu y los instructores de clase forman un círculo en el que la venerable Gran Madre Vientaguilar sigue ofreciendo consejo, guiando a los jóvenes recién iniciados a medida que asumen su papel como defensores de la Madre Tierra.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="Young shaman take their very first steps along the spiritual path here, undertaking trials to earn their Earth Totem and speak directly with the elementals of the mesa.",["race:Tauren"]="For the tauren, Camp Narache represents childhood's end—the sacred earth where you take your first rites of the hunt and attune yourself to the ancestral spirits under the watchful gaze of the Hawkwind elders."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Camp Narache is the starting village for young tauren, located atop Red Cloud Mesa in southern Mulgore. It is the central encampment of the Hawkwind tribe, serving as a sanctuary where fledgling hunters, warriors, druids, and shamans master their crafts before traveling outward to Bloodhoof Village and Thunder Bluff.",["al"]={"what is camp narache","narache lore","tauren starting town"},["q"]="What is Camp Narache?"},{["a"]="Chief Hawkwind guides the tribe's braves and coordinates the defenses of the mesa, alongside the tribe's revered elder, Greatmother Hawkwind. The tribe's trainers and elders gather at the center of the camp to instruct young adventurers.",["al"]={"who leads camp narache","camp narache chief","hawkwind leader"},["q"]="Who leads the village?"},{["a"]="The encampment is continually harassed by Bristleback quilboar operating out of Brambleblade Ravine to the east. In addition to feral battleboars and striders wandering the surrounding bluffs, the lingering danger of predatory centaur bands keeps the Hawkwind braves on constant alert.",["al"]={"camp narache enemies","who attacks camp narache","mesa threats"},["q"]="What threats does the camp face?"},{["a"]="Red Cloud Mesa is naturally bounded by sheer cliffs. The only way down into the greater plains of Mulgore is along a guarded mountain path leading north, watched over by Hawkwind braves to prevent hostile beasts and quilboar from ambushing travelers.",["al"]={"leaving red cloud mesa","exit camp narache","path off the mesa"},["q"]="Can travelers easily leave the mesa?"}},["kw"]={"bristleback","greatmother hawkwind","hawkwind","mulgore","narache","red cloud mesa","spirit lounge","tauren"},["n"]="Camp Narache",["s"]="Camp Narache is a secluded village nestled upon Red Cloud Mesa in southern Mulgore. It serves as the ancestral home of the Hawkwind tribe and the proving ground where young tauren begin their training. Sheltered high above the plains, the camp maintains ancient traditions while constantly guarding against encroaching quilboar and lingering centaur threats.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated at the northern edge of the elevated Red Cloud Mesa, Camp Narache is the primary settlement of the Hawkwind tribe. The village consists of several large hide lodges and pavilions, including a communal tent for wounded braves, an armory, a bakery tent, and a spirit lounge dedicated to meditation and ancestral communion. At the center of the camp, tribal elders and path trainers stand in a circle at the heart of the camp, where the venerable Greatmother Hawkwind still offers guidance, guiding newly initiated youth as they step into their roles as defenders of the Earth Mother.",["t"]="Heart of the Hawkwind Tribe"},{["b"]="Though naturally fortified by the steep sheer cliffs of the mesa, Camp Narache faces persistent unrest. Bristleback quilboar from Brambleblade Ravine continuously encroach upon Hawkwind lands, while centaur scouts linger in the distance. Young hunters, shamans, druids, and warriors prove their mettle here by culling the aggressive local wildlife, protecting the village's water well, and turning back quilboar raiders before descending the grand path into the wider valleys of Mulgore.",["t"]="A Proving Ground Under Threat"}}}}}
t["subzone:camp-taurajo"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,303,25.441.0,21.173.0,30.146.0,47.189.0",["h"]="741966",["n"]="Campamento Taurajo",["s"]="Campamento Taurajo. El Campamento Taurajo es un tranquilo asentamiento tauren enclavado en el sur de Los Baldíos, situado justo junto al paso de montaña que conduce al oeste hacia Mulgore. Sirve como un refugio fronterizo vital, ofreciendo a los caminantes cansados una posada, suministros, instructores de profesión y transporte en jinete del viento entre las llanuras y el centro de Kalimdor. Situado en la boca oriental del paso a Mulgore, el Campamento Taurajo suele ser el primer vistazo a la inmensidad de Los Baldíos que tienen los jóvenes tauren que se aventuran desde el Poblado Pezuña de Sangre. Rodeado de matorrales secos y mesetas escarpadas, el campamento funciona como puesto de avanzada y centro comercial. Da cobijo a cazadores, peleteros y herboristas de campo, al tiempo que mantiene conexiones de jinetes del viento con Cima del Trueno, El Cruce y el Poblado Viento Libre más al sur.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Camp Taurajo secures a critical overland junction and flight path, binding Mulgore closely to the rest of Horde-controlled central Kalimdor.",["race:Tauren"]="For tauren journeying out of Mulgore for the very first time, Camp Taurajo is the first friendly sanctuary encountered on the harsh plains of the Barrens."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Camp Taurajo is a tauren outpost and settlement in the southern Barrens, acting as a crucial waypoint between the homeland of Mulgore and the arid scrublands of the Barrens.",["al"]={"camp taurajo overview","what is taurajo","taurajo lore"},["q"]="What is Camp Taurajo?"},{["a"]="Following the dirt trail west past Camp Taurajo leads through the mountain pass into Mulgore, directly toward Bloodhoof Village and Thunder Bluff.",["al"]={"taurajo west pass","road west of camp taurajo","path to mulgore"},["q"]="Where does the road west lead?"},{["a"]="The local flight master coordinates wyvern routes connecting the camp directly to the Crossroads to the north, Thunder Bluff to the west, and Freewind Post in Thousand Needles to the south.",["al"]={"taurajo flight master","taurajo flight paths","flight connections taurajo"},["q"]="Where do the wind riders from Camp Taurajo fly?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","bloodhoof village","camp taurajo","mulgore pass","southern barrens","taurajo","tauren outpost"},["n"]="Camp Taurajo",["s"]="Camp Taurajo is a quiet tauren settlement nestled in the southern Barrens, sitting right along the mountain pass leading west into Mulgore. It serves as a vital frontier haven, offering tired wanderers an inn, supplies, profession mentors, and wind rider transit between the plains and central Kalimdor.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated at the eastern mouth of the pass to Mulgore, Camp Taurajo is often the first glimpse of the wider Barrens seen by young tauren venturing out from Bloodhoof Village. Surrounded by dry scrubland and rugged mesas, the camp operates as both an outpost and a trading hub. It shelters hunters, leathercrafters, and field herbalists while maintaining wind rider connections to Thunder Bluff, the Crossroads, and Freewind Post deeper south.",["t"]="Frontier of the Red Rocks"}}}}}
t["subzone:canals-stormwind-city"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="23,257,23.546.0,38.519.0,49.299.0,50.245.0,46.151.0,63.154.0",["h"]="f934f4",["n"]="Canales (Ciudad de Ventormenta)",["s"]="Canales (Ciudad de Ventormenta). Los Canales son una red de vías fluviales bordeadas de piedra que serpentean por Ciudad de Ventormenta, separando sus distintos distritos. Sirven como vías de paso tranquilas para peatones y pescadores, a la vez que albergan discretamente peligros ocultos y la entrada a la prisión de la ciudad. Los Canales conectan y definen los distritos de Ventormenta, dividiendo los bulliciosos mercados del Distrito de Mercaderes de los antiguos callejones del Casco Antiguo, los jardines de la catedral y el Distrito de los Enanos. Puentes de piedra, arcos y paseos junto al agua enmarcan establecimientos tranquilos como Bodega Gallina, sastrerías y serenas viviendas residenciales. Además de servir a comerciantes locales y pescadores aficionados, las vías fluviales ocultan la entrada fortificada a Las Mazmorras, donde los criminales y rebeldes más peligrosos de Ventormenta están recluidos bajo el nivel de la calle.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The canals stand as a testament to the rebuilding of the capital by the Alliance of Lordaeron, having transformed the choked, corpse-ridden ruins of the First War back into a functional, picturesque city.",["profession:Cooking"]="The quiet canal banks provide convenient spots for aspiring chefs to practice fishing for fresh catches without ever leaving the safety of the capital's walls."},["faq"]={{["a"]="When the Orcish Horde conquered and sacked Stormwind in the First War, the waterways were left filled with broken stone, timber, and rotting bodies. The retaking forces of the Alliance of Lordaeron had to painstakingly dredge the canals and properly bury the fallen before the city could be rebuilt.",["al"]={"canal history","canals first war","stormwind sack canals"},["q"]="What happened to the canals during the First War?"},{["a"]="No one can say for certain. Persistent urban legends tell of a massive white crocolisk lurking in the waterways. City guards and residents often dismiss it as tavern gossip, but the reports keep coming, and adventurers are warned not to fall in.",["al"]={"stormwind crocodile","canal alligator","sewer beast","white crocolisk"},["q"]="Is there really a monster in the Stormwind canals?"},{["a"]="The Stockade entrance is located along the northernmost stretch of the canal surrounding the Mage Quarter, guarded heavily by the Stormwind City Guard.",["al"]={"where is stockade","stockade entrance","how to get to stockade"},["q"]="Where is the entrance to the Stockade located?"},{["a"]="Swimming the canals is entirely possible, though getting back out onto the street requires finding stone stairs or docks spaced along the waterside paths.",["al"]={"swimming in canals","travel by water stormwind","water route stormwind"},["q"]="Can players swim through the canals to travel around Stormwind?"}},["kw"]={"canal district","canals","crocolisk","gallina","sewers","stockade","stormwind","waterways"},["n"]="Canals (Stormwind City)",["s"]="The Canals are a network of stone-lined waterways weaving through Stormwind City, separating its distinct districts. They serve as quiet thoroughfares for pedestrians and anglers, while quietly harboring hidden hazards and the entrance to the city's prison.",["sec"]={{["b"]="The Canals link and define the districts of Stormwind, dividing the bustling markets of the Trade District from the aged alleys of Old Town, the cathedral gardens, and the Dwarven District. Stone bridges, archways, and waterside walkways frame quiet establishments like the Gallina Winery, tailor shops, and quiet residential homes. In addition to serving local merchants and recreational fishermen, the waterways conceal the fortified entrance to the Stockade, where Stormwind's most dangerous criminals and rebels are held beneath street level.",["t"]="Arteries of the Capital"},{["b"]="The placid surface of the waterways belies a violent past. Following the sack of Stormwind during the First War, the canals were discovered choked with rubble, timber, and the corpses of slaughtered defenders. When the Alliance of Lordaeron liberated the ruins, soldiers undertook the grim labor of clearing the waterways and burying the dead before rebuilding began. Today, while cleaned and restored, the depths retain an air of mystery, fueled by city rumors of a massive albino crocolisk prowling beneath the docks.",["t"]="A Gruesome History and Lurking Shadows"}}}}}
t["subzone:canals-undercity"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,261,12.614.0,39.201.0,37.192.0,45.217.0",["h"]="5fb28c",["n"]="Canales (Entrañas)",["s"]="Canales (Entrañas). Los Canales forman un foso turbio y circular que serpentea entre los distintos barrios de Entrañas. Llenos de un limo verde, nocivo y antinatural en lugar de agua dulce, sirven tanto de sistema de alcantarillado como de sombrío símbolo de la fortaleza subterránea de los Renegados. Excavados en las profundidades subterráneas bajo las Ruinas de Lordaeron, los Canales rodean el corazón de Entrañas, dividiendo sus barrios con anchos cauces de fango verde y viscoso. Mientras que las ciudades de los mortales canalizan el agua corriente de los ríos para limpiar sus avenidas, los Renegados han llenado estos conductos de piedra con desechos industriales, vertidos químicos y residuos alquímicos. El líquido emite un brillo tenue y enfermizo, además de vapores pestilentes, lo que imposibilita cruzarlo mediante métodos mágicos ordinarios como Caminar sobre el agua. A pesar de la letalidad de esta masa cenagosa, pescadores desesperados extraen ocasionalmente curiosidades extrañas y corrompidas de entre el lodo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="The elements hold little sway over the polluted muck filling the Undercity's waterways, causing conventional spells like Water Walking to fail entirely.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the foul canals are entirely harmless to their unliving physiology, serving as a functional moat and chemical runoff channel suited to their subterranean realm."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is an alchemical sludge composed of toxic runoff, plague byproducts, and industrial waste that collects within the Undercity's drainage system. Unlike clean water, it is visibly tainted and noxious.",["al"]={"undercity green water","what is the slime in undercity","green slime river"},["q"]="What is the green liquid in the canals?"},{["a"]="Yes, patient anglers can cast a line into the sludge. Along with sickly, contaminated fish, people occasionally haul up discarded junk, including old human skulls from Lordaeron's fallen past.",["al"]={"fishing undercity","can you fish here","fishing in green slime"},["q"]="Can you fish in the Undercity canals?"},{["a"]="The thick, chemical slurry does not behave like natural water. Its foul viscosity and unnatural composition prevent shamans and other spellcasters from holding surface tension through conventional water-walking magic.",["al"]={"water walking undercity","shaman water walking bug","why cant i walk on water undercity"},["q"]="Why doesn't Water Walking work on the canals?"}},["kw"]={"canals","fishing","forsaken","green slime","lordaeron","sludge","toxic","undercity"},["n"]="Canals (Undercity)",["s"]="The Canals form a murky, circular moat winding between the distinct quarters of the Undercity. Filled with an unnatural, noxious green slime rather than fresh water, they serve as both a sewage system and a grim symbol of the Forsaken's subterranean stronghold.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Carved into the subterranean depths beneath the ruins of Lordaeron, the Canals encircle the heart of the Undercity, dividing its quarters with wide channels of sluggish green sludge. While mortal cities channel flowing river water to clean their avenues, the Forsaken have filled these stone conduits with industrial refuse, chemical runoff, and alchemical waste. The liquid emits a faint, sickly glow and foul vapors, making it impossible to traverse by ordinary magical means like water walking. Despite the lethality of the slurry, desperate anglers occasionally haul bizarre, tainted curiosities from the muck.",["t"]="A Toxic Moat"}}}}}
t["subzone:cathedral-of-light"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,249,25.559.0,26.550.0,42.241.0,51.278.0,38.212.0,41.245.0",["h"]="bd5269",["n"]="Catedral de la Luz",["s"]="Catedral de la Luz. La Catedral de la Luz es el corazón espiritual de la Ciudad de Ventormenta y el santuario principal de la Iglesia de la Luz Sagrada. Alzándose sobre la Plaza de la Catedral, sirve como bastión central para el sacerdocio humano y los Caballeros de la Mano de Plata. Reconstruida tras su devastación durante la Primera Guerra bajo la guía del Arzobispo Alonsus Faol y el por entonces obispo Benedictus, la Catedral de la Luz se erige como un imponente faro de resiliencia. Sus vastas salas y catacumbas subterráneas albergaron a refugiados desesperados durante las horas más oscuras de la reconstrucción de Ventormenta. Con la caída de Lordaeron ante la Plaga durante la Tercera Guerra, la sede de la Iglesia se trasladó al sur, a Ventormenta. Hoy en día, el Arzobispo Benedictus guía a los fieles desde esta gran sala, brindando guía espiritual a toda la Alianza.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="The Cathedral of Light serves as your principal order hall in Stormwind, where mentors like Duthorian Rall and Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker guide you through the sacred trials of the Tomes of Valor and Divinity.",["class:Priest"]="As the supreme seat of the Church of the Holy Light in the southern kingdoms, the cathedral is where High Priestess Laurena and Archbishop Benedictus nurture your spiritual devotion and sacred healing arts."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Archbishop Benedictus serves as the head of the Church of the Holy Light. Following the fall of Lordaeron and the demise of Archbishop Alonsus Faol, Benedictus assumed spiritual leadership over the reformed Church from his dais in Stormwind.",["al"]={"cathedral leader","who is the archbishop","who leads the church"},["q"]="Who leads the Church inside the cathedral?"},{["a"]="The cathedral serves as the operational headquarters of the Knights of the Silver Hand in the kingdom of Stormwind. Renowned paladins like Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker and Duthorian Rall instruct new squires, bestow sacred tomes, and direct crusaders against enemies of the realm.",["al"]={"silver hand stormwind","paladin order stormwind","why are paladins here"},["q"]="What is the cathedral's connection to the paladins?"},{["a"]="Beneath the main sanctuary lie ancient catacombs. Historically used as a shelter for refugees during the First and Second Wars, they now serve as the final resting place for honored heroes, priests, and paladins.",["al"]={"cathedral basement","cathedral catacombs","what is under the cathedral"},["q"]="What lies beneath the cathedral floor?"},{["a"]="The great bell tolling from the cathedral was forged upon the Great Forge in Ironforge. Crafted alongside a twin bell meant for Lordaeron, it was gifted to humanity by the dwarves as a testament to the enduring friendship between their kingdoms.",["al"]={"cathedral bell lore","who made the bell"},["q"]="Where did the cathedral's bell come from?"}},["kw"]={"benedictus","cathedral of light","cathedral square","duthorian rall","holy light","laurena","shadowbreaker","silver hand","stormwind"},["n"]="Cathedral of Light",["s"]="The Cathedral of Light is the spiritual heart of Stormwind City and the primary sanctuary of the Church of the Holy Light. Standing tall over Cathedral Square, it serves as the central bastion for human priesthood and the Knights of the Silver Hand.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Rebuilt after its devastation during the First War under the guidance of Archbishop Alonsus Faol and then-Bishop Benedictus, the Cathedral of Light stands as a towering beacon of resilience. Its vast halls and subterranean catacombs sheltered desperate refugees during the darkest hours of Stormwind's reconstruction. With the fall of Lordaeron to the Scourge during the Third War, the seat of the Church shifted south to Stormwind. Today, Archbishop Benedictus shepherds the faithful from this grand hall, providing spiritual guidance to the entire Alliance.",["t"]="Sanctuary of the Faithful"},{["b"]="Beyond serving as a house of prayer and healing, the cathedral acts as the primary headquarters for the remaining Knights of the Silver Hand in the southern kingdoms. High-ranking figures such as Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker and Duthorian Rall train promising squires through the sacred trials of the Tome of Valor and the Tome of Divinity. Alongside them, High Priestess Laurena guides devout acolytes in the deepest tenets of the Light, preparing holy champions to defend the realm against the rising threat of the Defias Brotherhood and the Scourge.",["t"]="Halls of Devotion and Arms"}}}}}
t["subzone:cathedral-square"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,300,17.492.0,26.571.0,25.241.0,31.201.0,36.216.0,33.205.0",["h"]="e53d6a",["n"]="Plaza de la Catedral",["s"]="Plaza de la Catedral. La Plaza de la Catedral es el corazón cívico y espiritual de la Ciudad de Ventormenta, presidido por la majestuosa Catedral de la Luz. Más allá de servir como lugar de culto y devoción, esta animada plaza alberga instituciones municipales como el ayuntamiento, el orfanato de la ciudad y el cuartel general regional del Alba Argenta. Situada al noroeste del Distrito de Mercaderes y al sureste del Distrito de los Enanos, Plaza de la Catedral sirve como el epicentro de la fe en el Reino de Ventormenta. Dominando el horizonte se alza la Catedral de la Luz, el santuario preeminente para los devotos de la Luz Sagrada en todo Azeroth. Sacerdotes, paladines y sanadores se reúnen aquí para estudiar, orar y entrenar. Ciudadanos, peregrinos y escolares locales guiados por la Maestra de escuela Danna se mezclan habitualmente en la plaza para conversar y meditar.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="For paladins, Cathedral Square is the fountainhead of faith and duty, housing mentors, sacred vows, and specialized armorers tailored to holy warriors.",["class:Priest"]="The quiet halls and towering spires of the square offer priests a tranquil sanctuary to commune with the Holy Light, advance their spiritual studies, and minister to the citizens of Stormwind."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Cathedral Square is a major district in Stormwind City centered on the Cathedral of Light. It serves as both the spiritual hub for practitioners of the Light and a vital civic center housing City Hall, the local orphanage, and various shops.",["al"]={"cathedral district","holy district","what is this place"},["q"]="What is Cathedral Square?"},{["a"]="Priests and Paladins of the Alliance come to Cathedral Square and the Cathedral of Light to hone their skills and study sacred doctrines. Medics and caregivers also study here under First Aid trainers.",["al"]={"class trainers here","who trains here","paladin priest trainers"},["q"]="Who trains in Cathedral Square?"},{["a"]="The Argent Dawn maintains a prominent embassy in Cathedral Square to recruit able-bodied champions and coordinate logistical support from Stormwind for their relentless crusade against the Scourge in the Plaguelands.",["al"]={"argent dawn stormwind","argent dawn presence"},["q"]="Why is the Argent Dawn located here?"},{["a"]="Bridges and canal paths link Cathedral Square directly to the bustling Trade District to the southeast, the industrial Dwarven District to the northwest, and the quiet gardens of the Park to the southwest.",["al"]={"connected districts","where does this go"},["q"]="Where does Cathedral Square lead?"}},["kw"]={"argent dawn","cathedral of light","cathedral square","city hall","holy district","orphanage","paladin","priest","stormwind"},["n"]="Cathedral Square",["s"]="Cathedral Square is the spiritual and civic heart of Stormwind City, dominated by the majestic Cathedral of Light. Beyond serving as a place of worship and devotion, the bustling plaza houses municipal institutions like City Hall, the city orphanage, and the regional headquarters of the Argent Dawn.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated northwest of the Trade District and southeast of the Dwarven District, Cathedral Square serves as the epicenter of faith in the Kingdom of Stormwind. Dominating the skyline is the Cathedral of Light, the preeminent sanctuary for followers of the Holy Light across Azeroth. Priests, paladins, and healers gather here to study, pray, and train. Citizens, pilgrims, and local schoolchildren led by School Mistress Danna regularly mingle in the square for conversation and contemplation.",["t"]="The Holy District"},{["b"]="The district is not merely reserved for prayer; it is one of the capital's busiest civic centers. The square houses the Stormwind Orphanage as well as City Hall, anchoring the administrative life of the kingdom. Specialized armorers and weaponsmiths catering to holy crusaders, such as Righteous Plates and Just Maces, line the avenues. It also serves as the base of operations for the Argent Dawn within Stormwind, where recruiters and representatives coordinate relief efforts and rally champions against the encroaching threats of the Scourge in the northern kingdoms.",["t"]="Civic Heart and Holy Order"}}}}}
t["subzone:cavern-of-mists"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,268,30.540.0,29.223.0,37.134.0,25.180.0,26.141.0",["h"]="66dec1",["n"]="Caverna de las Brumas",["s"]="Caverna de las Brumas. La Caverna de las Brumas es la amplia antecámara exterior que conduce a las profundidades de las Cuevas de los Lamentos. Alimentada por géiseres subterráneos que brotan a través de la roca, su poza central y su densa niebla albergan una extraña fauna mutada que merodea justo fuera del umbral del portal. Antes de descender al verdadero corazón de las Cuevas de los Lamentos, los viajeros deben abrirse paso por la Caverna de las Brumas. Un vapor denso y cálido flota permanentemente en el aire, alimentado por géiseres naturales que brotan del suelo de la caverna hacia una profunda poza central. Aunque sirve como entrada, dista mucho de ser un lugar apacible. Manadas de raptores, serpientes, mocos y trilladones semiacuáticos deambulan por las cornisas y las aguas, junto a bestias tristemente célebres como la hidra Trigore el Azotador. Ofrece a los aventureros un sombrío anticipo del crecimiento antinatural que se corrompe en las profundidades.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="The twisted wildlife thriving in the heavy vapors gives Cenarion druids their first warning of how deeply Naralex's Emerald Dream communion has gone astray.",["faction:Horde"]="Resting right in the heart of the Barrens, clearing out the predatory beasts lurking in these mists is critical to securing the trade routes and outposts around the Crossroads."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Cavern of Mists comprises the outer cave system of the Wailing Caverns, located southwest of the Crossroads in the Barrens. It is the non-instanced chamber that players must traverse to reach the instance portal itself.",["al"]={"cavern of mists location","where is cavern of mists","wailing caverns entrance cave"},["q"]="Where is the Cavern of Mists?"},{["a"]="Active geysers constantly burst from the stone floor, feeding the central pool and filling the subterranean air with heavy, humid fog.",["al"]={"why misty","cavern of mists name origin"},["q"]="Why is it called the Cavern of Mists?"},{["a"]="The chamber is populated by raptors, oozes, wind serpents, snakes, toads, and threshadons inhabiting the pool, as well as occasional sightings of the rare hydra Trigore the Lasher.",["al"]={"mobs in cavern of mists","cavern of mists monsters"},["q"]="What creatures live here?"},{["a"]="Trigore the Lasher is a dangerous rare hydra that can occasionally be found swimming alongside the threshadons in the chamber's central pool.",["al"]={"trigore","hydra rare wailing caverns"},["q"]="Who is Trigore the Lasher?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","cavern of mists","geysers","threshadons","trigore the lasher","wailing caverns"},["n"]="Cavern of Mists",["s"]="The Cavern of Mists is the expansive outer antechamber leading into the depths of the Wailing Caverns. Fed by subterranean geysers that erupt through the rock, its central pool and hanging fog harbor strange, mutated wildlife roaming just outside the portal threshold.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before descending into the true heart of the Wailing Caverns, travelers must navigate the Cavern of Mists. Thick, warm vapor hangs permanently in the air, fed by natural geysers erupting from the cavern floor into a deep central pool. Though it serves as an entryway, it is far from peaceful. Swarms of raptors, serpents, oozes, and semi-aquatic threshadons wander the ledges and waters, alongside notorious beasts like the hydra Trigore the Lasher. It provides adventurers an ominous preview of the unnatural growth festering deeper below.",["t"]="The Threshold of the Nightmare"}}}}}
t["subzone:champions-hall"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,396,31.625.0,37.124.0,42.230.0,35.212.0,46.154.0",["h"]="b27d18",["n"]="Sala de los Campeones",["s"]="Sala de los Campeones. Escondida en los confines meridionales del Casco Antiguo, la Sala de los Campeones sirve como cuartel de oficiales y armería de suministros para los veteranos condecorados de la Alianza en Ventormenta. Tras cruzar su umbral, los intendentes proporcionan armas especializadas, armaduras de placas y distintivos a los guerreros consagrados de la facción. El acceso está estrictamente custodiado y reservado únicamente para aquellos oficiales que hayan demostrado su valor en el campo de batalla. Oculta tras una entrada vigilada en el Casco Antiguo, la Sala de los Campeones es un refugio exclusivo para los combatientes más distinguidos de la Alianza. Los mandos militares se reúnen aquí ante mapas tácticos de Azeroth para deliberar sobre las campañas en curso, rodeados de armamento y las insignias honoríficas de su rango. Solo aquellos soldados que hayan ascendido en la jerarquía militar de la Alianza hasta alcanzar el estatus de oficial —concretamente el rango de Knight o superior— tienen permitida la entrada. En su interior, los intendentes militares suministran a los curtidos soldados armas de élite, armaduras y monturas fabricadas expresamente para decantar la balanza contra la Horda en los territorios en disputa de todo el mundo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="For front-line combatants, the hall represents the ultimate military stockpile, offering heavy battle gear and armaments reserved only for proven battlefield leaders.",["faction:Alliance"]="The hall stands as the premier symbol of Alliance military merit in Stormwind, honoring those who dedicate their lives to repelling Horde incursions."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Champions' Hall is located in the southern section of Old Town in Stormwind City, tucked away behind a guarded entrance.",["al"]={"where is champions hall","pvp vendor stormwind location","how to find champions hall"},["q"]="Where is the Champions' Hall located?"},{["a"]="Only Alliance veterans who have earned the military rank of Knight (Rank 6) or higher through the faction's honor system are granted passage through the entrance portal. Unproven recruits and civilians are barred at the threshold.",["al"]={"can anyone enter","champions hall requirements","why cant i enter champions hall"},["q"]="Who is allowed inside the Champions' Hall?"},{["a"]="The hall contains quartermasters offering officer-tier weapons, armor, insignia, and specialized war mounts. Alliance tacticians and generals also congregate around war tables lined with regional maps of Azeroth.",["al"]={"what does champions hall have","what vendors are in champions hall","champions hall rewards"},["q"]="What is inside the Champions' Hall?"},{["a"]="The Horde counterpart is the Hall of Legends, situated in Orgrimmar, which provides identical military supply services to decorated warriors of the Horde.",["al"]={"horde version of champions hall","orgrimmar pvp room","horde pvp barracks"},["q"]="What is the Horde equivalent of this building?"}},["kw"]={"champions hall","grand marshal","knight","officer barracks","old town","pvp vendors","quartermaster","stormwind"},["n"]="Champions' Hall",["s"]="Tucked away in the southern reaches of Old Town, the Champions' Hall serves as the officer's barracks and supply armory for the Alliance's decorated veterans in Stormwind. Beyond its threshold, quartermasters dispense specialized weapons, plate, and regalia to proven warriors of the faction. Access is strictly guarded, reserved only for officers who have demonstrated valor on the field of war.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Hidden behind a guarded threshold in Old Town, the Champions' Hall is a restricted haven for the Alliance's most distinguished combatants. Military commanders gather here over tactical maps of Azeroth to confer on ongoing campaigns, flanked by armaments and the grand insignias of rank. Only soldiers who have climbed the Alliance hierarchy to achieve officer status—specifically the rank of Knight or higher—are permitted entry. Inside, military quartermasters supply battle-hardened soldiers with elite arms, armor, and mounts crafted specifically to turn the tide against the Horde in contested zones across the world.",["t"]="The Alliance Officer's Barracks"}}}}}
t["subzone:charred-vale"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,275,19.499.0,20.411.0,32.249.0,48.216.0,40.172.0,50.122.0",["h"]="d2ebe8",["n"]="La Vega Carbonizada",["s"]="La Vega Carbonizada. La Vega Carbonizada es un valle humeante en el suroeste de Sierra Espolón, devastado por la tala imprudente y la maquinaria de Ventura y Cía. Antaño un próspero refugio para antárboles y quimeras, ahora está envuelto en llamas, elementales errantes y arpías hostiles. No hace mucho tiempo, esta cuenca del suroeste era un floreciente bosque alpino custodiado por majestuosos antárboles y habitado por quimeras y arpías autóctonas. Su ruina comenzó con la llegada de Ventura y Cía. La codiciosa organización de goblins taló por completo el bosque con maquinaria explosiva, corrompiendo a los guardianes y despertando a caóticos elementales de fuego. Aunque los antárboles acabaron haciendo retroceder a los goblins, la tierra quedó quebrantada, marcada por el fuego y mancillada por los viles artefactos que desplegaron los leñadores en su retirada.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="The devastation here serves as a harsh warning of what happens when natural balance is shattered by uncontrolled greed, making the valley a key focus for reclamation efforts.",["faction:Horde"]="Operating out of Sun Rock Retreat, Horde forces work closely with Cenarion allies to contain the elemental unrest and push back the corruptive lingering aftermath of the Venture Company."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The devastation was caused by the Venture Company's ruthless logging operations. Their destructive machinery and aggressive deforestation enraged the primal spirits of the land and unleashed destructive fire elementals that spread across the valley.",["al"]={"why is it burning","who burned charred vale","what happened to charred vale"},["q"]="Why is the Charred Vale on fire?"},{["a"]="Tauren druids from nearby Sun Rock Retreat believe it can. They task travelers with soothing the maddened treants and planting enchanted earthen seeds amidst the ash, hoping to coax green shoots from the ruined soil.",["al"]={"is charred vale healing","druids charred vale"},["q"]="Can the forest in the Charred Vale ever recover?"},{["a"]="The basin is crawling with hostile elemental fire spirits, blackened and vengeful ancients, Scorched Basilisks, and wild chimaeras. It is also plagued by Bloodfury harpies.",["al"]={"monsters in charred vale","what lives in charred vale"},["q"]="What creatures inhabit the Charred Vale?"},{["a"]="Its original name has been lost to time, but it was renowned as a lush woodland sanctuary long before goblin axes arrived.",["al"]={"charred vale old name","original name of charred vale"},["q"]="What was the Charred Vale called before it burned?"}},["kw"]={"blackened ancient","bloodfury","charred vale","chimaera","fire elemental","stonetalon","sun rock retreat","venture company"},["n"]="Charred Vale",["s"]="The Charred Vale is a smoldering valley in southwestern Stonetalon Mountains, devastated by the reckless deforestation and machinery of the Venture Company. Once a thriving haven for treants and chimaeras, it is now engulfed in flames, roving elementals, and hostile harpies.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Not long ago, this southwest basin was a flourishing alpine wood guarded by majestic treants and inhabited by native chimaeras and harpies. Its ruin began with the arrival of the Venture Company. The greedy goblin outfit clear-cut the forest with explosive machinery, corrupting the guardians and awakening chaotic fire elementals. Though the treants eventually forced the goblins back, the land was left broken, scarred by fire, and tainted by whatever foul devices the retreating loggers deployed.",["t"]="A Scorched Woodland"},{["b"]="Today, blackened ancients wander blindly through smoke and ash alongside enraged elementals. Bloodfury harpies roost in the skeletal snags, defending what remains of their territory. Despite the hostility of the valley, druids from Sun Rock Retreat refuse to abandon the region, dispatching travelers to sow enchanted seeds and tend the corrupted ancients in a persistent campaign to reclaim the scorched earth.",["t"]="Struggles of Renewal"}}}}}
t["subzone:chill-breeze-valley"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,303,30.543.0,37.192.0,49.302.0,42.178.0",["h"]="8aa9bd",["n"]="Valle Escalofrío",["s"]="Valle Escalofrío. El Valle Escalofrío es un paso escarpado y cubierto de nieve situado en el oeste de Dun Morogh que conecta el asentamiento enano de Kharanos con la asediada ciudad de Gnomeregan. Aunque su camino principal es una vía muy transitada por jóvenes viajeros y refugiados, sus apartados rincones albergan peligrosas bestias y sangrientas guaridas. El Valle Escalofrío forma una trinchera en forma de T a través de las montañas del oeste de Dun Morogh. El sendero principal de este a oeste registra un tránsito constante de enanos y gnomos novatos que viajan entre Kharanos y las afueras de Gnomeregan. Sin embargo, adentrarse en la ramificación norte-sur del valle es un asunto completamente diferente. Repletas de manchas de sangre y cadáveres destrozados, estas sombrías zonas albergan feroces depredadores, sobre todo salvajes wendigos que anidan en profundas cuevas de hielo y cazan a cualquiera lo bastante imprudente como para adentrarse en sus cotos de caza.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Dwarf"]="Mountaineers and young dwarven hunters test their mettle clearing out the ferocious wendigos that menace the vital passage connecting central Dun Morogh to the western highlands.",["race:Gnome"]="For gnomish refugees fleeing the fallout of Gnomeregan toward the safety of Kharanos and Ironforge, surviving the trek through Chill Breeze Valley's predatory perimeter is a critical first step."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Chill Breeze Valley is situated in western Dun Morogh, positioned directly between the bustling mountain hub of Kharanos to the east and the technological gnome city of Gnomeregan to the west.",["al"]={"chill breeze valley location","where is chill breeze valley","chill breeze valley map"},["q"]="Where is Chill Breeze Valley located?"},{["a"]="While the main path between Kharanos and Gnomeregan is relatively safe and heavily traveled, the northern and southern offshoots of the valley are hunting grounds for predatory beasts. The snow there is stained with blood and torn carcasses, leading to caves inhabited by vicious, territorial wendigos.",["al"]={"chill breeze valley monsters","dangers in chill breeze valley","why are there bones here"},["q"]="Why is the valley so dangerous to travel through?"},{["a"]="The deeper recesses of the valley are home to ferocious wendigos, including particularly large and elite alpha beasts that have claimed several cave dens as their personal lairs.",["al"]={"wendigo in chill breeze valley","what lives in chill breeze valley"},["q"]="What kinds of beasts make their dens here?"}},["kw"]={"caves","chill breeze valley","dun morogh","gnomeregan","kharanos","t-shaped","wendigo"},["n"]="Chill Breeze Valley",["s"]="Chill Breeze Valley is a rugged, snow-covered pass in western Dun Morogh linking the dwarven settlement of Kharanos with the embattled city of Gnomeregan. While its main path is a well-traveled thoroughfare for young travelers and refugees, its secluded recesses harbor dangerous beasts and bloody dens.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Chill Breeze Valley forms a T-shaped trench through the mountains of western Dun Morogh. The main east-west trail sees steady foot traffic from novice dwarves and gnomes journeying between Kharanos and the outskirts of Gnomeregan. However, straying into the valley's north-south offshoot is another matter entirely. Strewn with bloodstains and mangled carcasses, these shadowy reaches harbor ferocious predators—most notably savage wendigos that lair in deep ice caves and prey on anyone reckless enough to wander into their hunting grounds.",["t"]="A Crossroads of Snow and Claws"}}}}}
t["subzone:cleft-of-shadow"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,315,24.573.0,21.326.0,50.318.0,69.162.0,49.191.0",["h"]="42dc95",["n"]="Circo de las Sombras",["s"]="Circo de las Sombras. Oculto en las profundidades de las cavernas subterráneas bajo Orgrimmar, Circo de las Sombras alberga a quienes practican el sigilo, la hechicería y la demonología en la ciudad. Lejos del orgulloso espíritu guerrero de los distritos superiores de Thrall, sirve como un refugio necesario para pícaros, brujos y magos que operan en las sombras de la Horda. Aunque la nueva Horda de Thrall defiende el honor, el chamanismo y la fuerza de las armas, un liderazgo práctico exige un lugar para artes más sutiles. Excavado en las húmedas cavernas de piedra bajo la capital, Circo de las Sombras acoge a la Hermandad Shadowswift de pícaros, al Enclave Darkfire de brujos y a los eruditos del Enclave Arcano. Apartado del ajetreo diario de los distritos del valle, este sombrío barrio permite a quienes manejan venenos, energía vil y magia arcana ejercer sus oficios lejos de la vista pública directa, mientras permanecen bajo la atenta mirada de los líderes de Orgrimmar.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="The Shadowswift Brotherhood gathers here alongside poison merchants and lockpickers, turning this dark recess into the primary den for the Horde's stealth operatives.",["class:Warlock"]="The Darkfire Enclave gives Horde warlocks a sanctioned place to summon demons and bind fel energy beneath Orgrimmar without drawing the immediate wrath of shaman and warriors."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Thrall strives to keep the Horde united under honorable shamanic and warrior traditions. While the utility of warlocks and rogues is acknowledged, their practices are distrusted by much of the orcish public. Confining them to the subterranean caverns keeps dangerous fel and illicit activities contained and monitored.",["al"]={"why cleft of shadow","why warlocks underground orgrimmar","cleft of shadow lore"},["q"]="Why are warlocks and rogues kept underground here?"},{["a"]="The cavern serves as Orgrimmar's primary hub for rogue, warlock, and mage trainers. It also hosts poison suppliers, reagent vendors, and wand and staff merchants.",["al"]={"trainers in cleft of shadow","who is in cleft of shadow"},["q"]="What major trainers and services can be found in the Cleft of Shadow?"},{["a"]="The chasm plunging into the cavern floor leads to Ragefire Chasm, a perilous subterranean network of lava tubes beneath Orgrimmar infested with troggs, searing elementals, and rogue cultists.",["al"]={"dungeon in cleft of shadow","cleft cave entrance","what instance is here"},["q"]="What is the entrance at the bottom of the cavern?"}},["kw"]={"arcane enclave","cleft of shadow","darkfire enclave","mage","orgrimmar","ragefire chasm","rogue","shadowswift brotherhood","warlock"},["n"]="Cleft of Shadow",["s"]="Tucked deep within the subterranean caverns beneath Orgrimmar, the Cleft of Shadow houses the city's practitioners of stealth, sorcery, and demonology. Far from the proud warrior ethos of Thrall's upper districts, it serves as a necessary haven for rogues, warlocks, and mages operating in the shadows of the Horde.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While Thrall's new Horde champions honor, shamanism, and strength of arms, practical leadership demands a place for subtler arts. Carved into the damp stone caverns below the capital, the Cleft of Shadow hosts the Shadowswift Brotherhood of rogues, the Darkfire Enclave of warlocks, and the scholars of the Arcane Enclave. Kept away from the everyday bustle of the valley districts, this dark quarter allows practitioners of poison, fel energy, and arcane magic to ply their trades out of direct public view while remaining under the watchful eye of Orgrimmar's leadership.",["t"]="A Subterranean Sanctuary"},{["b"]="Beyond acting as a center for covert instruction and magical reagents, the Cleft of Shadow descends directly into Ragefire Chasm. This fiery network of volcanic caves honeycombs beneath Orgrimmar itself, posing an ongoing security threat that draws adventurous defenders and sinister cultists alike right to the cavern's edge.",["t"]="A Dangerous Threshold"}}}}}
t["subzone:cliffspring-falls"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,417,16.682.0,26.197.0,49.225.0,42.181.0,51.218.0",["h"]="d3665f",["n"]="Salto de Fonrroca",["s"]="Salto de Fonrroca. El Salto de Fonrroca marca el espectacular origen del vital Río Fonrroca de Costa Oscura, precipitándose desde los acantilados orientales hacia el bosque costero. Celebrado durante mucho tiempo como la principal fuente de agua potable limpia para la región, sus aguas han sido víctimas recientemente de una vil y expansiva corrupción. La caverna subterránea que alimenta la cascada se ha infestado de hostiles nagas y sombríos cultores del Martillo Crepuscular. Brotando de cavernas encaramadas a gran altura en los riscos rocosos del borde oriental de Costa Oscura, el Salto de Fonrroca alimenta el Río Fonrroca, que serpentea hacia el oeste a través de los bosques hasta desembocar en el mar. Tradicionalmente, esta cascada proporcionaba el agua potable más pura para los asentamientos locales de elfos de la noche. En tiempos recientes, sin embargo, las aguas se han vuelto fétidas y turbias, propagando la enfermedad y el deterioro ecológico por toda la cuenca del río. Los naturalistas que investigan el suceso han descubierto que la red de cuevas en la cabecera de las cataratas está invadida por viles nagas y oscuros cultores, que conspiran entre las sombras mientras la corrupción demoníaca del vecino Frondavil amenaza con filtrarse a través del lecho rocoso de las tierras altas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Druids of the Cenarion Circle monitor the river closely, striving to diagnose and cleanse the unnatural rot that threatens to choke the wilderness.",["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei of Auberdine, the corruption of Cliffspring Falls is an environmental and spiritual crisis, polluting the vital waters that nourish Darkshore's ancient forests."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Cliffspring Falls is a major waterfall in eastern Darkshore that forms the headwaters of the Cliffspring River. It historically supplied the primary fresh drinking water for the surrounding forest.",["al"]={"cliffspring falls","cliffwater falls","what is cliffspring falls"},["q"]="What is Cliffspring Falls?"},{["a"]="Two sinister influences are suspected: demonic taint seeping through the mountains from corrupted Felwood, and the active presence of Twilight's Hammer cultists and hostile naga lurking inside the caverns feeding the cascade.",["al"]={"why is water tainted","cliffspring river corruption","corrupted water"},["q"]="Why is the water coming from the falls corrupted?"},{["a"]="The caverns above and behind the waterfall are infested with hostile naga slithering through the flooded chambers, alongside cultists belonging to the apocalyptic Twilight's Hammer.",["al"]={"who is in the caves","cliffspring cave mobs","who lives in cliffspring falls"},["q"]="Who occupies the caverns behind the falls?"},{["a"]="The Cliffspring River cuts through the center of northern Darkshore. Because it serves as the principal source of fresh water, its poisoning directly endangers wildlife, ancient groves, and local night elf habitations.",["al"]={"why does darkshore care","cliffspring importance"},["q"]="Why is Cliffspring Falls so important to Darkshore?"}},["kw"]={"auberdine","cliffspring falls","cliffspring river","cliffwater falls","darkshore","felwood","naga","twilight's hammer","water corruption"},["n"]="Cliffspring Falls",["s"]="Cliffspring Falls marks the dramatic origin of Darkshore's vital Cliffspring River, tumbling down from the eastern cliffs into the coastal forest. Long celebrated as the principal source of clean drinking water for the region, its waters have recently fallen victim to a foul, spreading taint. The subterranean cavern feeding the waterfall has become infested with hostile naga and shadowy Twilight's Hammer cultists.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Pouring out from caverns perched high in the rocky bluffs along Darkshore's eastern border, Cliffspring Falls feeds the Cliffspring River, which winds westward across the woods to empty into the sea. Traditionally, this cascade provided the purest drinking water for local night elf settlements. In recent times, however, the waters have turned foul and murky, spreading sickness and ecological decay throughout the river basin. Investigating naturalists have discovered that the cave network at the falls' headwaters is overrun by vile naga and dark cultists, who plot in the shadows while demonic corruption from neighboring Felwood threatens to seep through the highland bedrock.",["t"]="A Tainted Source"}}}}}
t["subzone:cold-hearth-manor"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,390,16.513.0,43.236.0,35.230.0,33.229.0,44.297.0",["h"]="aad4cb",["n"]="Mansión Fríogar",["s"]="Mansión Fríogar. La Mansión Fríogar es una granja asolada ubicada justo al oeste de Rémol, junto al camino principal de Claros de Tirisfal. Antaño una finca bulliciosa y hospitalaria conocida por sus abundantes cosechas, el brote de la Plaga de la Muerte aniquiló a sus residentes, dejando los campos circundantes plagados de miembros de la Plaga sin mente. En la actualidad, los Renegados han asegurado la casa de campo principal como puesto de avanzada y parada para los viajeros. Antes de la Tercera Guerra, esta granja gozaba de una reputación de calidez y hospitalidad, produciendo ricas cosechas en el corazón de Lordaeron. Cuando la Plaga arrasó el reino, la familia entera y sus trabajadores sucumbieron, alzándose de nuevo como cascarones atados a la Plaga. Aunque los muertos vivientes ferales todavía deambulan por los campos en ruinas, las fuerzas de los Renegados lograron expulsar a los muertos sin mente de la casa de campo principal, recuperando la estructura para que sirviera como puesto comercial y punto de apoyo a lo largo del camino hacia los claros del este.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="The manor offers a secure vantage along the road between Brill and the eastern reaches of Tirisfal, providing a safe waypoint for travelers navigating the plagued countryside.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, reclaiming places like Cold Hearth Manor is a bitter reminder of their lost mortal lives, converting former human sanctuaries into grim defensive outposts against both the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The farmers and workers who tended the estate were completely wiped out when the Plague of Undeath swept across Lordaeron. Rather than finding peace in death, they were raised as mindless zombies that still haunt the surrounding fields.",["al"]={"who lived at cold hearth","manor backstory","what happened to the family"},["q"]="What happened to the people who lived here?"},{["a"]="The estate originally had a reputation for its warm atmosphere and welcoming fires. The grim moniker was likely adopted by the Forsaken as an ironic nod to its former life, marking how cold, dead, and blighted the farm has become.",["al"]={"cold hearth name meaning","why cold hearth"},["q"]="Why is it called Cold Hearth Manor?"},{["a"]="The Forsaken have taken control of the primary farmhouse, using it as a safe stop for travelers and traders along the road from Brill. However, the open fields and barns surrounding the manor remain infested with hostile Scourge.",["al"]={"who owns cold hearth manor","is cold hearth friendly"},["q"]="Who controls the manor right now?"},{["a"]="The Forsaken in Tirisfal Glades are stretched thin, fighting off mindless Scourge remnants while warding off Scarlet Crusade crusaders. Securing the farmhouse and main road provides immediate utility, leaving the scattered dead in the fields as a nuisance rather than an immediate threat to Brill.",["al"]={"why are there zombies in the fields","why scourge here"},["q"]="Why don't the Forsaken clear out the fields?"}},["kw"]={"brill","cold hearth manor","farmstead","forsaken","scourge","tirisfal glades","zombies"},["n"]="Cold Hearth Manor",["s"]="Cold Hearth Manor is a blighted farmstead located just west of Brill along the main road of Tirisfal Glades. Once a bustling, hospitable estate known for bountiful crops, the outbreak of the Plague of Undeath wiped out its residents, leaving the surrounding fields choked with mindless Scourge. Today, the Forsaken have secured the main farmhouse as an outpost and waystation for travelers.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the Third War, this homestead bore a reputation for warmth and hospitality, supporting rich harvests in the heart of Lordaeron. When the Plague swept through the kingdom, the entire family and their laborers succumbed, rising again as husks bound to the Scourge. While feral undead still stumble through the ruined fields, Forsaken forces managed to push the mindless dead out of the main farmhouse, reclaiming the structure to serve as a trading post and foothold along the road toward the eastern glades.",["t"]="A Chilled Hearth"}}}}}
t["subzone:coldridge-pass"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,440,29.541.0,31.157.0,39.231.0,41.190.0,33.179.0",["h"]="b80d70",["n"]="Desfiladero de Crestanevada",["s"]="Desfiladero de Crestanevada. El Desfiladero de Crestanevada es un túnel escarpado y cubierto de nieve que atraviesa la cordillera montañosa meridional de Dun Morogh. Sirve como la única ruta terrestre que conecta los apartados campos de entrenamiento del Valle de Crestanevada con el resto del reino, desembocando cerca de la bulliciosa villa de Kharanos. Debido a que unos troggs hostiles han invadido el paso, cualquier viajero que intente cruzarlo debe abrirse camino luchando o emprender una carrera desesperada hacia el otro lado. Para los jóvenes reclutas enanos y los novicios gnomos que dan sus primeros pasos más allá del Valle de Crestanevada, el Desfiladero de Crestanevada es un duro rito de iniciación. Cincelado directamente a través de la roca, este túnel constituye el enlace principal que envía a los aventureros recién instruidos hacia el este, con rumbo al núcleo fronterizo de Kharanos. Lo que otrora fuera un corredor de montaña seguro se ha convertido en un peligroso cuello de botella, infestado de agresivos troggs que han emergido desde oscuros subterráneos para amenazar a cualquier alma que intente viajar entre el resguardado valle y las extensiones más amplias de Dun Morogh.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarven mountaineers and recruits, traversing Coldridge Pass represents your departure from novice training at Anvilmar into active service across Ironforge's lands.",["race:Gnome"]="Exiled gnomes seeking to aid the Alliance must push through this trogg-infested choke point to reach Kharanos and the higher road toward Ironforge."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The pass connects Coldridge Valley in the southwest to the greater region of Dun Morogh, emptying out into the snowy hills just west of the town of Kharanos.",["al"]={"where does coldridge pass go","coldridge pass destination","how to leave coldridge valley"},["q"]="Where does Coldridge Pass lead?"},{["a"]="Troggs have recently surged forth from the deep subterranean cracks beneath Dun Morogh, seizing dark caves and tunnels throughout the region. Coldridge Pass provided them shelter and an easy ambush point against mountain travelers.",["al"]={"why are troggs here","coldridge pass monsters","trogg infestation"},["q"]="Why are there troggs in Coldridge Pass?"},{["a"]="No, it is not safe. The tunnel is swarming with hostile troggs, meaning recruits and travelers must cut their way through the brutes or sprint through the darkness to reach the opposite end.",["al"]={"is coldridge pass dangerous","can i walk through coldridge pass"},["q"]="Is Coldridge Pass safe to travel through?"},{["a"]="Mountaineers watch the valley and road exits, but the tunnel interior remains contested and uncleared, leaving individual travelers to defend themselves as they make the crossing.",["al"]={"dwarf guards at coldridge pass","who controls the pass"},["q"]="Who guards or maintains the pass?"}},["kw"]={"anvilmar","coldridge pass","coldridge valley","dun morogh","kharanos","mountain pass","trogg","tunnel"},["n"]="Coldridge Pass",["s"]="Coldridge Pass is a rugged, snowbound tunnel cutting through the southern mountain ridge of Dun Morogh. It serves as the sole overland route connecting the secluded training grounds of Coldridge Valley to the rest of the kingdom, emerging near the bustling town of Kharanos. Because hostile troggs have overrun the passage, any traveler attempting the journey must either fight their way through or make a desperate dash for the other side.",["sec"]={{["b"]="For young dwarven recruits and gnome novices taking their first steps beyond Coldridge Valley, Coldridge Pass is a harsh rite of passage. Chiseled straight through the rock, this tunnel forms the primary link sending newly trained adventurers eastward toward the frontier hub of Kharanos. What was once a secure mountain corridor has become a perilous choke point, infested with aggressive troggs that have pushed up from dark sub-terrains to menace any soul trying to travel between the sheltered valley and the wider reaches of Dun Morogh.",["t"]="The Gateway Out of the Valley"}}}}}
t["subzone:coldridge-valley"] = {["faq"]={{["a"]="La única ruta terrestre para salir del valle discurre por el Desfiladero de Crestanevada, un túnel nevado que atraviesa la cordillera hacia el noreste. Una vez cruzado el desfiladero, el camino se dirige hacia el este, directo a la ciudad de Kharanos y en adelante hacia las grandes Puertas de Forjaz.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="8d0d22",["i"]=1,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Tras la trágica caída de Gnomeregan a manos de los troggs y la lluvia radiactiva, los gnomos supervivientes huyeron a Dun Morogh como refugiados. La gente del Manitas Mayor Mekkatorque fue acogida por el Rey Magni Barbabronce, lo que llevó a muchos aprendices gnomos exiliados a entrenar codo con codo con jóvenes enanos en Yunquemar.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="f6d572",["i"]=2,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="El valle se enfrenta a dos amenazas principales: los hostiles trols Peloescarcha, que resienten los asentamientos enanos en su territorio montañoso, y los toscos troggs Quijaroca, que han surgido de las entrañas de la tierra para bloquear el Desfiladero de Crestanevada. Los depredadores locales, como lobos y jabalíes, también hostigan a los viajeros desprevenidos.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="e29d20",["i"]=3,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Yunquemar es el pabellón fortaleza central y asentamiento del Valle de Crestanevada. Alberga a instructores de clase, maestros de forja y oficiales montaraces locales que coordinan la defensa del valle y preparan a los aventureros recién instruidos para adentrarse en el resto del mundo.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="60ad03",["i"]=4,["q"]="",["sp"]=0}},["fp"]="16,350,25.508.0,16.522.0,34.256.0,47.293.0,38.283.0,17.249.0",["h"]="203075",["n"]="Valle de Crestanevada",["s"]="Valle de Crestanevada. El Valle de Crestanevada es un valle resguardado y cubierto de nieve, situado en las alturas del suroeste de Dun Morogh. Articulado alrededor de la aldea de Yunquemar, sirve como campo de entrenamiento donde jóvenes enanos y gnomos refugiados toman las armas por primera vez al servicio de Forjaz. Un único túnel, el Desfiladero de Crestanevada, conecta esta hondonada aislada con el resto del reino montañoso. Cobijado por escarpados riscos montañosos, el Valle de Crestanevada permanece prácticamente aislado de las concurridas rutas comerciales de Dun Morogh. En su corazón se encuentra Yunquemar, un robusto salón de piedra y aldea donde veteranos instructores enanos y eruditos gnomos desplazados entrenan a los nuevos reclutas en las artes del combate, el sigilo y la hechicería. Fuera de la calidez de los hogares de Yunquemar, el suelo del valle está cubierto de una espesa capa de nieve y acechado por jabalíes y hambrientos lobos invernales, lo que brinda a los novatos su primera toma de contacto real con la supervivencia en la frontera.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Dwarf"]="As the traditional starting ground for Bronzebeard mountaineers and clerics, the valley represents a dwarf's first steps beyond the hearth and into service of the High Seat.",["race:Gnome"]="For gnome exiles forced from Gnomeregan, the snows of Coldridge Valley offer a safe haven to master their spells and machinery alongside their dwarven hosts."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The only overland route out of the valley leads through Coldridge Pass, a snowy tunnel cutting northeast through the mountain ridge. Once through the pass, the road heads east directly toward the town of Kharanos and onward to the great gates of Ironforge.",["al"]={"exit coldridge","how to get out","path to kharanos"},["q"]="How do you leave Coldridge Valley?"},{["a"]="Following the tragic fall of Gnomeregan to troggs and radioactive fallout, surviving gnomes fled into Dun Morogh as refugees. High Tinker Mekkatorque's people were welcomed by King Magni Bronzebeard, leading many exiled gnomish apprentices to train side by side with young dwarves in Anvilmar.",["al"]={"gnomes in coldridge","why are gnomes here","gnome starting area"},["q"]="Why are gnomes starting here alongside dwarves?"},{["a"]="The valley faces two major menaces: the hostile Frostmane trolls, who resent dwarven settlements on their mountain territory, and crude Rockjaw troggs, who have clawed up from the deep earth to choke Coldridge Pass. Local predators like wolves and boars also harass unwary travelers.",["al"]={"coldridge enemies","valley threats","who is attacking"},["q"]="What threats are troubling the valley?"},{["a"]="Anvilmar is the central fortress-lodge and settlement within Coldridge Valley. It houses class trainers, forge-masters, and local mountaineer officers who coordinate the defense of the valley and prepare newly forged adventurers for the wider world.",["al"]={"anvilmar town","what is the town here"},["q"]="What is Anvilmar?"}},["kw"]={"anvilmar","coldridge pass","coldridge valley","dun morogh","frostmane","ironforge","starting area","troggs"},["n"]="Coldridge Valley",["s"]="Coldridge Valley is a sheltered, snow-covered vale tucked into the southwestern heights of Dun Morogh. Centered around the hamlet of Anvilmar, it serves as the training ground where young dwarves and gnome refugees first take up arms in service of Ironforge. A single tunnel, Coldridge Pass, connects this secluded hollow to the wider mountain realm.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Cradled by sheer mountain cliffs, Coldridge Valley remains largely cut off from the bustling trade routes of Dun Morogh. At its heart sits Anvilmar, a sturdy stone hall and hamlet where veteran dwarven instructors and displaced gnome scholars train fresh recruits in the arts of battle, stealth, and sorcery. Outside the warmth of Anvilmar's hearths, the valley floor is carpeted in thick snow and prowled by boars and hungry winter wolves, providing novices with their first real taste of frontier survival.",["t"]="A Secluded Proving Ground"},{["b"]="Despite its isolation, Coldridge Valley faces immediate danger from two relentless enemies. Indigenous Frostmane trolls have established camps like the Frostmane Hovel, skirmishing with mountaineers and defending their ancestral claims against dwarven encroachment. Worse still, savage Rockjaw troggs have overrun Coldridge Pass, the natural tunnel linking the valley to Kharanos. Until these subterranean brutes are pushed back, travelers and supplies cannot freely move between the valley and the high seat of Ironforge.",["t"]="Encroaching Foes"}}}}}
t["subzone:command-center"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,366,22.537.0,22.335.0,35.248.0,57.166.0,28.168.0,36.134.0",["h"]="bf1c3e",["n"]="Centro de Mando",["s"]="Centro de Mando. El Centro de Mando, a menudo conocido como el Cuartel de Ventormenta, se alza en el corazón del Casco Antiguo como el cuartel general operativo de los oficiales militares de la ciudad. En tiempos de paz alberga al ejército permanente, pero con las fuerzas de Ventormenta desplegadas en fronteras distantes, actualmente opera con una dotación mínima de veteranos centrada en instruir a los reclutas y a la milicia local. Situado en las desgastadas calles del Casco Antiguo, el Centro de Mando sirve como la guarnición principal y el campo de entrenamiento marcial para el reino de Ventormenta. Aunque normalmente está repleto de infantería regular y oficiales de alto rango, las instalaciones se encuentran inusualmente vacías. Con gran parte del ejército real comprometido en campañas en el extranjero, el cuartel depende de un cuadro de instructores veteranos —incluidos Ander Germaine y el artista marcial Wu Shen— para adiestrar a los nuevos guerreros, mientras figuras como Wulf Hansreim entrenan a tiradores para reforzar las defensas de la ciudad.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="Marksmen visiting Stormwind report to the Command Center to learn techniques from veteran trainers such as Wulf Hansreim.",["class:Warrior"]="The Command Center is the primary hub in Stormwind for warrior training, where veterans like Ander Germaine and Wu Shen hone recruits into disciplined frontline soldiers."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Most of Stormwind's standing army has been deployed to distant outposts and foreign battlefields across the world. The Command Center currently maintains only a skeleton crew of seasoned veterans to instruct new recruits and organize local defense.",["al"]={"why few guards here","where is stormwind army","barracks empty"},["q"]="Why is the Command Center so empty?"},{["a"]="Yes. While officially designated the Command Center, city guards and local residents routinely refer to the building as the Stormwind Barracks when giving directions.",["al"]={"stormwind barracks","are command center and barracks the same","barracks location"},["q"]="Is the Command Center the same as the Stormwind Barracks?"},{["a"]="Ander Germaine coordinates and trains the city's warriors alongside instructors like Wu Shen and Ilsa Corbin, while Wulf Hansreim oversees hunter and marksman training.",["al"]={"who trains warriors here","warrior trainer command center","who runs the barracks"},["q"]="Who leads the training here?"},{["a"]="The Command Center is located in Old Town, situated near the Pig and Whistle Tavern and central to the district's training facilities.",["al"]={"where is command center","command center location","how to find command center"},["q"]="Where is the Command Center located?"}},["kw"]={"ander germaine","barracks","command center","hunter trainer","old town","stormwind barracks","warrior trainer","wu shen","wulf hansreim"},["n"]="Command Center",["s"]="The Command Center, often referred to as the Stormwind Barracks, stands in the heart of Old Town as the operational headquarters for the city's military officers. In peacetime, it houses the standing army, but with Stormwind's forces dispatched to distant frontiers, it currently operates with a seasoned skeleton crew focused on drilling recruits and local militia.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated within the weathered streets of Old Town, the Command Center serves as the primary garrison and martial training ground for the kingdom of Stormwind. Normally packed with regular infantry and ranking officers, the facility is uncharacteristically sparse. With much of the royal army committed to campaigns abroad, the barracks relies on a veteran cadre of instructors—including Ander Germaine and martial artist Wu Shen—to train fresh warriors, while figures like Wulf Hansreim drill marksmen to bolster the city's defenses.",["t"]="A Thin Line of Defense"},{["b"]="Guards throughout Stormwind often direct newcomers to the 'Barracks' when seeking instruction in heavy arms and tactical combat. The building's proximity to both the Pig and Whistle Tavern and the shadowy operations elsewhere in Old Town makes it an essential anchor of order in a district known for tavern brawls and roguish activity.",["t"]="Old Town's Martial Hub"}}}}}
t["subzone:craftsmen-s-terrace"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,341,30.508.0,31.454.0,51.235.0,58.239.0,41.160.0,53.199.0",["h"]="aa227e",["n"]="Bancal del Artesano",["s"]="Bancal del Artesano. El Bancal del Artesano es el bullicioso distrito artesanal situado en los confines septentrionales de Darnassus. Funciona como el principal centro comercial y manufacturero de la capital de los elfos de la noche, albergando talleres, instructores de profesión y una concurrida posada. El distrito también acoge a representantes externos, incluida una embajada de la facción neutral del Alba Argenta. Extendiéndose por el extremo norte de la ciudad de copas arbóreas, el Bancal del Artesano reúne los diversos oficios que mantienen en funcionamiento a Darnassus. Tallistas de madera, peleteros, alquimistas y otros artesanos gestionan aquí sus talleres, combinando los métodos tradicionales de los elfos de la noche con la artesanía práctica. El distrito también ofrece servicios comunitarios esenciales, como una posada, un maestro de hermandad y vendedores de peticiones de hermandad. Sendos puentes conectan el bancal directamente con el Enclave Cenarion al oeste y con el Bancal del Guerrero al sur.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance visitors find the terrace to be one of Darnassus's most welcoming quarters, offering familiar trade supplies, guild administration, and lodging alongside foreign representatives.",["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, the terrace is proof of their society's self-reliance on Teldrassil, blending ancient craftsmanship with the day-to-day needs of their new capital."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The district houses most of the city's trade profession trainers, craft supply merchants, an inn, and guild registry services. It serves as the commercial center for travelers looking to learn or practice practical skills in Darnassus.",["al"]={"craftsmen services","what is in craftsmens terrace","darnassus trainers"},["q"]="What services are found in the Craftsmen's Terrace?"},{["a"]="The Argent Dawn maintains an embassy in the district to liaise with the night elves and recruit aid against the Scourge. Their presence offers a diplomatic bridge between the Alliance forces in the west and the war-torn lands of Lordaeron.",["al"]={"argent dawn darnassus","argent dawn embassy","why argent dawn here"},["q"]="Why is the Argent Dawn present in the Craftsmen's Terrace?"},{["a"]="The terrace occupies the northern section of Darnassus. You can reach it via bridges leading north from the Warrior's Terrace or east from the Cenarion Enclave.",["al"]={"how to get to craftsmen terrace","craftsmen terrace location","finding craftsmen terrace"},["q"]="How do you reach the Craftsmen's Terrace?"},{["a"]="Scholarly volumes rest throughout the workshops, including histories of the War of the Ancients, the aftermath of the Second War, and a study on the Old Gods housed within the Argent Dawn's quarters.",["al"]={"craftsmen terrace books","lore books darnassus","books in craftsmens terrace"},["q"]="What notable books can be found around the workshops?"}},["kw"]={"argent dawn","artisans","craftsmen's terrace","craftsmens terrace","darnassus","teldrassil","trainers"},["n"]="Craftsmen's Terrace",["s"]="The Craftsmen's Terrace is the bustling artisan district situated in the northern reaches of Darnassus. It serves as the primary trade and manufacturing hub for the night elf capital, housing workshops, profession trainers, and a lively inn. The district also hosts external representatives, including an embassy for the neutral Argent Dawn.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Spanning the northern edge of the canopy city, the Craftsmen's Terrace gathers the diverse trades that keep Darnassus running. Woodworkers, leathercrafters, alchemists, and other artisans operate their shops here, integrating classic night elven methods with practical craft. The district also provides essential community amenities, including an inn, a guild master, and guild petition vendors. Bridges connect the terrace directly to the Cenarion Enclave to the west and the Warrior's Terrace to the south.",["t"]="The Artisan Heart of Darnassus"},{["b"]="Despite the kaldorei's historic isolation, the Craftsmen's Terrace is home to foreign connections, most notably an embassy established by the Argent Dawn to coordinate with northern allies against the Scourge. Visitors browsing the district's various workshops might also stumble across scattered scholarly volumes, ranging from historical accounts of the War of the Ancients to chronicles detailing the Second War and esoteric treatises on the Old Gods.",["t"]="Outside Ties and Forgotten Lore"}}}}}
t["subzone:crag-of-the-everliving"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="22,298,18.491.0,20.427.0,34.261.0,38.196.0,64.170.0,47.219.0",["h"]="db7dfe",["n"]="Risco del Eterno",["s"]="Risco del Eterno. El Risco del Eterno es una cámara cavernosa cubierta de vegetación enclavada en las profundidades de las Cuevas de los Lamentos. Dominada por una flora exuberante y corrupta junto a criaturas vegetales depredadoras, sirve como dominio del Noble del Colmillo Lord Pythas. Sus imponentes niveles superiores albergan a la entidad ancestral que da nombre al risco. Mientras que gran parte de las Cuevas de los Lamentos está excavada en piedra subterránea húmeda, el Risco del Eterno rebosa de una vegetación desmedida y retorcida alimentada por la Pesadilla que corrompe el letargo de Naralex. Imponentes plataformas musgosas y sinuosos senderos están abarrotados de arrastrapiés descarriados: moles vegetales vivientes que merodean por la maleza. Lord Pythas, uno de los discípulos caídos de Naralex, vigila los tramos centrales del risco, habiendo cambiado sus nobles votos druídicos por los ritos venenosos de los Druidas del Colmillo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Seeing the Crag of the Everliving is a tragic lesson for Cenarion druids, as pure natural vitality and elemental guardianship have been warped into lethal tools of the Nightmare.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The crag's unnaturally lush subterranean atmosphere nourishes rare underground roots and mushrooms that flourish in the humid, dream-soaked soil."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The chamber is named after Verdan the Everliving, an ancient and colossal plant beast residing in the highest terraces of the crag. Though once an embodiment of nature's timeless vitality, he has fallen under the sway of the Nightmare that afflicts the caverns.",["al"]={"why crag of the everliving","everliving name origin","crag name"},["q"]="Where does this area get its name?"},{["a"]="Lord Pythas, one of the primary Fanglords, directly presides over the crag. In the higher ledges above him lurk both Verdan the Everliving and Lord Serpentis, the leader of the Druids of the Fang.",["al"]={"who is in charge here","crag boss","fanglord here"},["q"]="Who controls this part of the caverns?"},{["a"]="The crag is overrun with Deviate Shamblers—shambling plant horrors birthed from the corrupted springs—alongside twisted serpents and the fanatical Druids of the Fang.",["al"]={"monsters in crag","crag enemies","what lives here"},["q"]="What creatures are commonly found in the Crag of the Everliving?"},{["a"]="The underground springs were harnessed by the night elf druid Naralex to rejuvenate the Barrens. When his ritual was snared by the Emerald Nightmare, the wild growth ran rampant and twisted into hostile, aberrant flora.",["al"]={"why are there plants underground","why so green","corrupted greenery"},["q"]="Why is plant life thriving so deep underground?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","crag of the everliving","deviate shamblers","druids of the fang","lord pythas","lord serpentis","verdan","wailing caverns"},["n"]="Crag of the Everliving",["s"]="The Crag of the Everliving is a verdant cavern chamber nestled deep within the Wailing Caverns. Dominated by lush, corrupted flora and predatory plant creatures, it serves as the domain of the Fanglord Lord Pythas. Its towering upper reaches shelter the ancient entity after whom the crag is named.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While much of the Wailing Caverns is carved of damp subterranean stone, the Crag of the Everliving bursts with unruly, twisted vegetation fueled by the Nightmare corrupting Naralex's slumber. Towering mossy platforms and winding paths are choked with Deviate Shamblers—living plant hulks prowling the undergrowth. Lord Pythas, one of Naralex's fallen disciples, watches over the crag's central reaches, having traded his noble druidic vows for the venomous rites of the Druids of the Fang.",["t"]="A Corrupted Canopy"},{["b"]="The chamber draws its name from Verdan the Everliving, a colossal, primordial plant elemental who resides in the crag's upper heights. Corrupted by the Emerald Nightmare that grips the cavern, Verdan now acts as a fearsome line of defense rather than a peaceful natural guardian. Beyond his towering form lurks Lord Serpentis, the self-proclaimed chief of the Fanglords, who oversees the sect's descent into serpentine madness.",["t"]="The Ancient Guardian"}}}}}
t["subzone:crossroads"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="10,336,32.539.0,28.538.0,48.251.0,48.198.0,58.253.0,46.184.0",["h"]="bbd602",["n"]="El Cruce",["s"]="El Cruce. El Cruce es el corazón del transporte de la Horda por el centro de Kalimdor, situado donde el Camino del Oro de norte a sur se cruza con la ruta que va desde Trinquete hasta Sierra Espolón. Sirve como un bullicioso puesto comercial, zona de preparación militar y centro de tránsito para los viajeros que se desplazan entre Durotar, Mulgore y los frentes del norte. Fiel a su nombre, El Cruce se asienta justo en la intersección del Camino del Oro y la ruta de este a oeste que cruza desde el puerto goblin de Trinquete hasta Sierra Espolón. A pesar de contar con alojamientos modestos, el puesto funciona como un bullicioso centro neurálgico regional. Maestros de jinetes del viento, comerciantes, herreros e instructores mantienen puestos permanentes bajo sus torres de vigilancia. Para los jóvenes guerreros que viajan desde Durotar o Mulgore, el asentamiento suele ser el primer lugar donde son testigos de la vasta logística en múltiples frentes que une a la nueva Horda.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Striking the Crossroads directly cuts off the flow of Horde reinforcements moving between Orgrimmar, Mulgore, and the disputed borders of Ashenvale.",["faction:Horde"]="The Crossroads is the central proving ground and crossroads of your fledgling nation, linking the homelands of the orcs, tauren, and trolls while coordinating supplies across Kalimdor."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It anchors the major transit arteries of central Kalimdor. Every traveler moving overland between Durotar, Mulgore, Ratchet, Stonetalon, or Ashenvale must pass through or near the Crossroads, making it the primary hub for logistics and reinforcements.",["al"]={"why is crossroads important","crossroads purpose","why crossroads matters"},["q"]="Why is the Crossroads so important to the Horde?"},{["a"]="Devrak serves as the flight master at the Crossroads, managing the settlement's wind rider roost and connecting travelers directly to outposts across Kalimdor, including Orgrimmar and Thunder Bluff.",["al"]={"crossroads flight master","who has wyverns here","flight master crossroads"},["q"]="Who provides flight transport at the Crossroads?"},{["a"]="Because the Crossroads is central to Horde transit and located within easy striking distance of both Ashenvale to the north and the neutral port of Ratchet to the east, Alliance raiding parties regularly target the outpost to disrupt Horde supply lines.",["al"]={"why alliance raids crossroads","alliance pvp crossroads","crossroads attacks"},["q"]="Why does the Alliance attack the Crossroads so frequently?"},{["a"]="Barrens raptors raided the Crossroads guard tower and made off with a shipment of silver intended to pay the settlement's defending guards, scattering it into the surrounding savannah.",["al"]={"stolen payroll crossroads","who took the silver","crossroads silver stolen"},["q"]="What happened to the outpost's payroll silver?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","crossroads","devrak","gold road","raptors","ratchet","stonetalon","wind rider"},["n"]="Crossroads",["s"]="The Crossroads is the beating heart of Horde travel through central Kalimdor, situated where the north-south Gold Road intersects the path from Ratchet to the Stonetalon Mountains. It serves as a bustling trading outpost, military staging area, and transit hub for travelers journeying between Durotar, Mulgore, and northern frontlines.",["sec"]={{["b"]="True to its name, the Crossroads sits squarely at the crossing of the Gold Road and the east-west route cutting from the goblin port of Ratchet into the Stonetalon Mountains. Despite having modest lodgings, the outpost functions as a bustling regional hub. Wind rider masters, merchants, blacksmiths, and trainers maintain permanent setups beneath its watchtowers. For young warriors traveling out from Durotar or Mulgore, the settlement is often the first place they witness the vast, multi-front logistics binding the new Horde together.",["t"]="A Vital Junction in the Savannah"},{["b"]="Maintaining order at the Crossroads is a relentless struggle. Local wildlife—including plains raptors bold enough to plunder payroll silver from the guard towers—poses a persistent nuisance, while harpies, quilboar, and centaur tribes continually pressure the perimeter. Beyond the threats native to the Barrens, the settlement's proximity to neutral Ratchet and the contested forests of Ashenvale makes it a prime target for encroaching Alliance scouting parties, leading to frequent skirmishes just outside its defensive barricades.",["t"]="Frontier Outpost Under Siege"}}}}}
t["subzone:crusader-outpost"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,340,18.492.0,31.433.0,29.184.0,26.156.0,41.232.0,31.150.0",["h"]="09704a",["n"]="Avanzada de los Cruzados",["s"]="Avanzada de los Cruzados. La Avanzada de los Cruzados es una torre de vigilancia fortificada situada en lo alto de las escarpadas colinas del este de los Claros de Tirisfal. Guarnecida por celosos miembros de la Cruzada Escarlata, vigila los accesos que conducen hacia su bastión en el Monasterio Escarlata. Desde esta altura, los cruzados observan el tránsito por el camino y están preparados para repeler cualquier incursión de los Renegados. Construida en los riscos que dominan el camino oriental, la Avanzada de los Cruzados sirve como principal estación de alerta temprana para la Cruzada Escarlata. Desde su elevada torre, los centinelas vigilan el movimiento entre Rémol y los confines orientales de Lordaeron, asegurándose de que los no-muertos errantes o los grupos de exploración sean avistados mucho antes de alcanzar las puertas del Monasterio. La torre también otorga a la guarnición la capacidad táctica de flanquear a cualquier fuerza que intente marchar valle arriba hacia su sagrado bastión.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Navigating the eastern trails of Tirisfal requires caution, as Scarlet sentries atop this hill will swiftly attack anyone traveling toward the Monastery.",["race:Undead"]="This watchtower sits right on the edge of Forsaken territory, serving as a bitter reminder that zealous living crusaders still hold sovereign pockets within the glades."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is a fortified scouting tower held by the Scarlet Crusade in eastern Tirisfal Glades. It monitors the road passing below and protects the southern approach to the Scarlet Monastery.",["al"]={"what is this tower","crusader outpost tirisfal","scarlet watchtower"},["q"]="What is the Crusader Outpost?"},{["a"]="The outpost is manned by zealots of the Scarlet Crusade under the command of Captain Vachon. They view all undead as abominations to be eradicated on sight.",["al"]={"who owns crusader outpost","who lives here","scarlet crusade outpost"},["q"]="Who controls this outpost?"},{["a"]="Its elevated position offers clear sightlines over the main eastern thoroughfare of Tirisfal Glades. This allows Crusaders to detect Forsaken troop movements early and flank any forces attempting an assault on the Scarlet Monastery.",["al"]={"why build here","outpost location","tactical purpose"},["q"]="Why is the tower situated in these hills?"},{["a"]="Yes. The Scarlet Crusade considers all outsiders—particularly the Forsaken and their Horde allies—corrupt enemies who must be purged in holy fire.",["al"]={"is crusader outpost hostile","are they aggressive"},["q"]="Will the guards here attack me?"}},["kw"]={"captain vachon","crusader outpost","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","scout tower","tirisfal glades","watchtower"},["n"]="Crusader Outpost",["s"]="Crusader Outpost is a fortified watchtower perched atop the rugged hills of eastern Tirisfal Glades. Manned by zealous members of the Scarlet Crusade, it guards the approaches leading toward their stronghold at the Scarlet Monastery. From this height, Crusaders observe travel along the road and stand ready to repel any Forsaken incursion.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Built into the bluffs overlooking the eastern road, the Crusader Outpost serves as a primary early-warning station for the Scarlet Crusade. From their elevated tower, sentries watch over movement between Brill and the eastern reaches of Lordaeron, ensuring that wandering undead or scouting parties are spotted long before reaching the Monastery gates. The tower also grants the garrison tactical flanking capability against any force seeking to march up the valley toward their holy bastion.",["t"]="Eyes Over Tirisfal"},{["b"]="Under the command of Scarlet officers like Captain Vachon, the garrison stationed here maintains unwavering vigilance. They see the surrounding woods not as sovereign territory of the Forsaken, but as unhallowed soil stolen from humanity by monstrosities. For travelers loyal to the Undercity, the outpost represents an ever-present ambush point where crossbow bolts and cleansing steel await anyone straying too close to the bluffs.",["t"]="A Thorn in the Dark Lady's Side"}}}}}
t["subzone:crystal-lake"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,248,16.478.0,17.352.0,30.154.0,41.227.0,41.198.0,43.203.0",["h"]="7e06ed",["n"]="Lago de Cristal",["s"]="Lago de Cristal. El Lago de Cristal es una masa de agua situada justo al este de Villadorada, en el corazón del Bosque de Elwynn. Aunque antaño era un lugar tranquilo, sus costas han sido invadidas por agresivos múrlocs, convirtiéndose en un peligro habitual para los lugareños y los viajeros de paso. Situado a poca distancia a pie de la Posada Orgullo de León, el Lago de Cristal debería ser un idílico retiro rural, pero está plagado de fauna peligrosa. Tribus de múrlocs de agua dulce se han apoderado de la orilla y de los bajíos, atacando a cualquiera que se acerque demasiado. El alquimista local William Mortero contrata con frecuencia a los aventureros que pasan por allí para que se aventuren hasta la orilla del agua, indicándoles que derroten a las criaturas y recolecten las algas de cristal que portan para utilizarlas en sus brebajes experimentales.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The murloc infestation so close to Goldshire underscores how thinly stretched the kingdom's military has become in safeguarding its core territories.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The freshwater shallows harbor Crystal Kelp, though it is primarily gathered directly from the resident murlocs who harvest it from the lake bed."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Crystal Lake lies directly east of the crossroads town of Goldshire in central Elwynn Forest, easily reached by walking past the outskirts of the village.",["al"]={"crystal lake location","where is crystal lake","find crystal lake"},["q"]="Where is Crystal Lake located?"},{["a"]="Like many waterways in Elwynn Forest, Crystal Lake provides a natural freshwater habitat where murlocs can nest and forage. Their numbers have swelled close to Goldshire due to the strained resources of Stormwind's local guard.",["al"]={"why murlocs crystal lake","murloc problem goldshire","crystal lake murlocs"},["q"]="Why are murlocs gathered at Crystal Lake?"},{["a"]="The grave marker on the central island reads only 'Deeply missed, never forgotten.' There is no name etched upon the stone, leaving the identity of the person buried there an enduring local mystery.",["al"]={"crystal lake grave","tombstone on island elwynn","who is buried at crystal lake"},["q"]="Whose grave is on the island in the lake?"},{["a"]="William Pestle, an apothecary working out of Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, contracts adventurers to slay the murlocs along the shore to gather crystal kelp, which he requires for an invisibility potion.",["al"]={"william pestle crystal lake","kelp quest crystal lake","invisibility potion elwynn"},["q"]="What do adventurers need from Crystal Lake?"}},["kw"]={"crystal kelp","crystal lake","elwynn","goldshire","grave","jason mathers","murloc","william pestle"},["n"]="Crystal Lake",["s"]="Crystal Lake is a body of water lying just east of Goldshire in the heart of Elwynn Forest. While once a peaceful spot, its shores have been overrun by aggressive murlocs, turning it into a frequent hazard for local villagers and passing travelers.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated within walking distance of Lion's Pride Inn, Crystal Lake should be an idyllic rural retreat, but it is plagued by dangerous wildlife. Tribes of freshwater murlocs have claimed the shoreline and shallow shoals, attacking anyone who strays too close. Local alchemist William Pestle frequently hires passing adventurers to venture to the water's edge, directing them to defeat the creatures and harvest the crystal kelp they carry for use in his experimental concoctions.",["t"]="A Troubled Shore"},{["b"]="Resting quietly in the center of the lake is a tiny, isolated islet. Solitary and overgrown, it bears a simple grave marked with the tender inscription: 'Deeply missed, never forgotten.' The identity of whoever rests beneath the soil remains unrecorded in town ledgers, providing a somber mystery amidst the surrounding croaks of the shoreline murlocs.",["t"]="The Silent Island"}}}}}
t["subzone:cut-throat-alley"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,287,15.663.0,35.264.0,48.219.0,37.189.0,41.146.0",["h"]="5a1bf5",["n"]="Callejón de los Degolladores",["s"]="Callejón de los Degolladores. Callejón de los Degolladores es un rincón apartado y deshabitado de la Ciudad de Ventormenta, oculto tras las tiendas de los canales. Escondido detrás de un establecimiento llamado La Dama Sombría, cerca del límite con Distrito de los Enanos, consta de un patio tranquilo y una residencia vacía aislada del tránsito habitual de la ciudad. Callejón de los Degolladores es uno de los rincones más silenciosos y reservados de Ventormenta. Aunque técnicamente figura cartografiado junto al Distrito de los Enanos, no comparte en absoluto los rugientes fuegos de las forjas ni el denso hollín de dicho distrito. No se puede acceder al callejón desde ninguna de las avenidas principales de la ciudad; el único paso a pie atraviesa directamente La Dama Sombría, una pequeña tienda situada junto a los canales, justo al sur del puente de la Plaza de la Catedral. Tras la puerta del comercio se halla un pequeño callejón sin salida pavimentado, repleto de cajas apiladas, barriles olvidados y una única residencia desocupada de dos plantas. Completamente oculto a la vista de los guardias que patrullan y de los ciudadanos corrientes, reposa en absoluto silencio en medio del bullicio de la capital.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="Accessible only through the rear door of a shady canal shop, this unpatrolled dead-end offers an ideal hideout for anyone who prefers to stay out of sight of the Stormwind City Guard."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Head to the canal front along the edge of the Dwarven District, just south of the footbridge leading to Cathedral Square. Look for a shop named the Shady Lady. Walking straight through the back of this establishment brings you right out into the tucked-away alley.",["al"]={"find cut throat alley","cut throat alley location","where is cut-throat alley","how to enter cut-throat alley"},["q"]="How do you get to Cut-Throat Alley?"},{["a"]="The outdoor passage shares the broader Dwarven District subzone label on common maps. The name 'Cut-Throat Alley' only reveals itself on your compass once you step inside the empty two-story home at the back of the lot.",["al"]={"minimap dwarven district","why does it say dwarven district","cut-throat alley name bug"},["q"]="Why does the map call this the Dwarven District?"},{["a"]="No. The alley and its lone two-story house are completely abandoned. Aside from stacked cargo crates and empty barrels, there are no residents, shopkeepers, or city watchmen stationed here.",["al"]={"cut throat alley npcs","who lives in cut throat alley","empty house cut throat alley"},["q"]="Is anyone living in Cut-Throat Alley?"},{["a"]="There are no formal duties or civic assignments that lead into the alley. It serves purely as an overlooked, secluded backdrop within the capital.",["al"]={"cut throat alley quests","cut throat alley storyline"},["q"]="Are there any quests in Cut-Throat Alley?"}},["kw"]={"cathedral square","cut-throat alley","dwarven district","secret alley","shady lady","stormwind canals"},["n"]="Cut-Throat Alley",["s"]="Cut-Throat Alley is a secluded, unpopulated back corner of Stormwind City hidden away behind the canal shops. Tucked behind a storefront called the Shady Lady near the Dwarven District border, it consists of a quiet courtyard and an empty residence cut off from normal city foot traffic.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Cut-Throat Alley is one of Stormwind's quietest and most secretive corners. Though technically charted alongside the Dwarven District, it shares none of the district's roaring forge fires or heavy soot. The alley cannot be reached from any of the city's main avenues; the only foot path leads straight through the Shady Lady, a small shop lining the canals just south of the bridge from Cathedral Square. Beyond the shop door lies a small paved dead-end lined with stacked crates, forgotten barrels, and a single unoccupied two-story residence. Completely hidden from passing guards and ordinary citizens, it sits entirely silent amidst the bustle of the capital.",["t"]="A Secluded Nook"}}}}}
